INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(8546,'https://reliefweb.int/report/sudan/refugee-settlement-environmental-degradation-nexus-kassala-el-gedaref-and-white-nile-states-sudan-november-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/sudan/refugee-settlement-environmental-degradation-nexus-kassala-el-gedaref-and-white-nile-states-sudan-november-2026','Refugee Settlement-Environmental Degradation Nexus in Kassala, El Gedaref, and White Nile States, Sudan (November 2026)','refugeesettlementenvironmentaldegradationnexusinkassalaelgedarefandwhitenilestatessudannovember2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-03T02:04:13Z','2026-11-03T04:11:17Z','Countries: Sudan, Central African Republic, Eritrea, Ethiopia, South Sudan, Syrian Arab Republic Source: CGIAR Please refer to the attached file. Citation Mekuria, Wolde, Rediet Girma, and Awdenegest Moges. 2026. Refugee Settlement-Environmental Degradation Nexus in Kassala, El Gedaref, and White Nile States, Sudan. International Water Management Institute (IWMI). Abstract/Description Sudan hosts some of Africa''s largest and longest-standing refugee populations in fragile drylands already strained by unreliable rainfall, land degradation, and conflict. This study examines whether refugee settl',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(8547,'https://reliefweb.int/report/lebanon/lebanon-food-security-outlook-update-insecurity-and-weak-livelihood-recovery-sustain-crisis-ipc-phase-3-outcomes-october-2026-may-2027','https://reliefweb.int/report/lebanon/lebanon-food-security-outlook-update-insecurity-and-weak-livelihood-recovery-sustain-crisis-ipc-phase-3-outcomes-october-2026-may-2027','Lebanon Food Security Outlook Update: Insecurity and weak livelihood recovery sustain Crisis (IPC Phase 3) outcomes, October 2026 - May 2027','lebanonfoodsecurityoutlookupdateinsecurityandweaklivelihoodrecoverysustaincrisisipcphase3outcomesoctober2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-03T01:01:41Z','2026-11-03T04:11:17Z','Countries: Lebanon, Syrian Arab Republic Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages Crisis (IPC Phase 3) outcomes are expected to persist through May 2027 across South, El-Nabatieh, Baalbek–El-Hermel, Akkar, and parts of North and Bekaa. Ongoing insecurity-related livelihood disruptions in the south, limited income-earning opportunities, and high food and fuel costs will continue to constrain household purchasing power and food access among poor Lebanese households, Syrian refugees, and internally displaced populations. Insecurity continues to d',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(8548,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/why-geohazards-must-be-part-pacifics-resilience-agenda','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/why-geohazards-must-be-part-pacifics-resilience-agenda','World: Why geohazards must be part of the Pacific’s resilience agenda','worldwhygeohazardsmustbepartofthepacificsresilienceagenda','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-03T00:28:16Z','2026-11-03T04:11:17Z','Countries: World, Tonga, Vanuatu Sources: Pacific Community, UN Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific, UN Office for Disaster Risk Reduction Please refer to the attached file. For years, global discussions of disaster risk in the Pacific have been dominated by climate change. Rising seas, intensifying cyclones and coastal erosion have rightly captured international attention. This focus, while warranted, should be complemented by greater recognition of geohazards, which are just as consequential and in many cases, more immediately devastating. Addressing this gap requires a m',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(8549,'https://reliefweb.int/report/burkina-faso/west-africa-seasonal-monitor-rainy-season-draws-end-deficits-observed-chad-niger-and-mali-october-30-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/burkina-faso/west-africa-seasonal-monitor-rainy-season-draws-end-deficits-observed-chad-niger-and-mali-october-30-2026','Burkina Faso: West Africa Seasonal Monitor: Rainy season draws to an end with deficits observed in Chad, Niger, and Mali (October 30, 2026)','burkinafasowestafricaseasonalmonitorrainyseasondrawstoanendwithdeficitsobservedinchadnigerandmalioctober302026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-02T21:03:09Z','2026-11-03T04:11:17Z','Countries: Burkina Faso, Chad, Mali, Niger, Nigeria Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages During the second dekad of October, the Intertropical Front (ITF) retreated southward along its entire length, indicating that the rainy season is coming to an end across the Sahel. Rainfall deficits have persisted throughout the rainy season, with the most severe deficits recorded in the Sahelian zones of Chad, Niger, and Mali. Moderate deficits have also been observed in Burkina Faso and northeastern Nigeria. These rainfall deficits have hindered cro',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(8550,'https://reliefweb.int/report/afghanistan/afghanistan-seasonal-monitor-above-average-precipitation-and-above-normal-temperatures-are-expected-early-2026-27-wet-season','https://reliefweb.int/report/afghanistan/afghanistan-seasonal-monitor-above-average-precipitation-and-above-normal-temperatures-are-expected-early-2026-27-wet-season','Afghanistan Seasonal Monitor: Above-average precipitation and above-normal temperatures are expected early in the 2026-27 wet season','afghanistanseasonalmonitoraboveaverageprecipitationandabovenormaltemperaturesareexpectedearlyinthe202627wetseason','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-02T19:03:07Z','2026-11-03T04:11:17Z','Country: Afghanistan Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages The CHIRPS-GEFS short-term forecast indicates cumulative precipitation across most of the country will remain near average (within +/- 10 mm) through November 10, 2026. Exceptions include isolated areas in the northeast and east, where precipitation deficits of 10–25 mm below average are possible, and isolated locations in the southeast along the Pakistan border, where precipitation surpluses of 10–25 mm above average are forecast ( Figure 1 ). The Copernicus Climate Change Services',6.0,'classified',NULL,259);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(8551,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/undrr-escwa-and-league-arab-states-advance-regional-cooperation-disaster-statistics-risk-informed-decision-making','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/undrr-escwa-and-league-arab-states-advance-regional-cooperation-disaster-statistics-risk-informed-decision-making','World: UNDRR, ESCWA, and League of Arab States Advance Regional Cooperation on Disaster Statistics for Risk-Informed Decision-Making','worldundrrescwaandleagueofarabstatesadvanceregionalcooperationondisasterstatisticsforriskinformeddecisionmaking','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-02T04:03:09Z','2026-11-03T04:11:17Z','Country: World Source: UN Office for Disaster Risk Reduction The United Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction (UNDRR), the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Western Asia (ESCWA), and the League of Arab States convened a three-day Regional Workshop on Disaster-Related Statistics in Cairo from 27 to 29 October 2026, bringing together representatives of national disaster management authorities, statistical offices, and regional and international organizations. Under the theme “Strengthening disaster data systems for evidence-based policymaking and anticipatory action,” the wo',2.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
