INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9437,'https://reliefweb.int/report/sri-lanka/sri-lanka-food-security-outlook-october-2026-may-2027-widespread-stressed-ipc-phase-2-through-january-ahead-maha-harvest','https://reliefweb.int/report/sri-lanka/sri-lanka-food-security-outlook-october-2026-may-2027-widespread-stressed-ipc-phase-2-through-january-ahead-maha-harvest','Sri Lanka Food Security Outlook, October 2026 - May 2027: Widespread Stressed (IPC Phase 2) through January ahead of maha harvest','srilankafoodsecurityoutlookoctober2026may2027widespreadstressedipcphase2throughjanuaryaheadofmahaharvest','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-05T02:55:17Z','2026-11-05T04:11:19Z','Country: Sri Lanka Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages Widespread Stressed (IPC Phase 2) outcomes are expected from October through January (the lean season) as yala stocks begin to decline, and households become increasingly market dependent amid elevated food, fuel, transportation, and other essential costs. Second inter-monsoon and northeast monsoon rains will likely cause flooding, high winds, landslides, and rough seas, which will periodically disrupt agricultural and fishing activities. Resulting impacts to income, compounded by hig',8.0,'classified',NULL,290);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9438,'https://reliefweb.int/report/south-sudan/who-weekly-situation-update-ongoing-health-emergency-events-south-sudan-week-44-date-26-oct-1-nov-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/south-sudan/who-weekly-situation-update-ongoing-health-emergency-events-south-sudan-week-44-date-26-oct-1-nov-2026','WHO Weekly Situation Update on Ongoing Health Emergency Events in South Sudan - Week #44, Date: 26 Oct - 1 Nov 2026','whoweeklysituationupdateonongoinghealthemergencyeventsinsouthsudanweek44date26oct','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-05T00:25:34Z','2026-11-05T04:11:19Z','Countries: South Sudan, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya, Nigeria Source: World Health Organization Please refer to the attached file. PRIORITY ACTIONS Sustain BVD preparedness across the priority counties as DRC reaches 10,467 cases and 5,103 deaths (CFR 48.8%); maintain PoE screening (81,967 events over 31 Oct–2 Nov) and screen air arrivals at Juba International Airport. Investigate the new Juba (Munuki) alert — a Ugandan trader who died on 2 Nov with fever and profuse bleeding after travel to eastern DRC. Operationalize the WHO El Niño health plan (1 Nov–30 Apr): pre-position cholera',2.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9439,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/global-weather-hazards-summary-november-05-2026-november-11-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/global-weather-hazards-summary-november-05-2026-november-11-2026','World: Global Weather Hazards Summary, November 05, 2026 – November 11, 2026','worldglobalweatherhazardssummarynovember052026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-04T20:33:05Z','2026-11-05T04:11:19Z','Country: World Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Global Overview : El Niño continues to strengthen. Rainfall deficits are present in parts of equatorial Africa, northwestern Central Asia, across most of Central America, in some areas of Hispaniola, and in much of northern South America. Africa Weather Hazards Hot conditions are expected across parts of the Sahel, western Eastern Africa, and Southern Africa; while high flooding risks exist over eastern South Africa. 1) The Sudd wetlands of South Sudan continue to experience inundation. 2) A large par',6.0,'classified',NULL,289);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9440,'https://reliefweb.int/report/mozambique/mozambique-learns-japans-expertise-disaster-risk-reduction','https://reliefweb.int/report/mozambique/mozambique-learns-japans-expertise-disaster-risk-reduction','Mozambique learns from Japan’s expertise in disaster risk reduction','mozambiquelearnsfromjapansexpertiseindisasterriskreduction','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-04T12:33:10Z','2026-11-05T04:11:19Z','Countries: Mozambique, Japan Source: UN Office for Disaster Risk Reduction How can countries invest today to reduce disaster losses tomorrow? A delegation from Mozambique explored this question during a study tour and workshop in Japan, learning how centuries of experience, strategic investment and technological innovation can help reduce disaster risks and strengthen resilience. Mozambique faces recurring cyclones, floods, droughts and storm surges that continue to threaten lives, livelihoods and critical infrastructure. As the country works to strengthen its disaster risk reduction mechanism',1.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9441,'https://reliefweb.int/report/tunisia/arab-states-mark-iddrr-2026-through-regional-cooperation-and-community-led-preparedness','https://reliefweb.int/report/tunisia/arab-states-mark-iddrr-2026-through-regional-cooperation-and-community-led-preparedness','Tunisia: Arab States Mark IDDRR 2026 Through Regional Cooperation and Community-Led Preparedness','tunisiaarabstatesmarkiddrr2026throughregionalcooperationandcommunityledpreparedness','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-04T12:33:08Z','2026-11-05T04:11:19Z','Countries: Tunisia, Oman, Qatar, Syrian Arab Republic Source: UN Office for Disaster Risk Reduction Arab States mark IDDRR 2026 with regional dialogue and community-led preparedness initiatives Across the Arab region, governments, local authorities, civil society organizations, and communities marked the International Day for Disaster Risk Reduction (IDDRR) on 13 October 2026 under the theme “Resilience Starts at Home.” Activities in Tunisia, Syria, Qatar, and Oman highlighted the importance of strengthening disaster preparedness, promoting inclusive early warning systems, and empowering commu',4.0,'classified',NULL,283);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9442,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/el-nino-preparedness-anticipatory-action-framework-city-leaders','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/el-nino-preparedness-anticipatory-action-framework-city-leaders','World: El Niño Preparedness: An Anticipatory Action Framework for City Leaders','worldelninopreparednessananticipatoryactionframeworkforcityleaders','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-04T09:34:16Z','2026-11-05T04:11:19Z','Country: World Source: Intergovernmental Authority on Development Please refer to the attached Infographic. An advisory note by UN-Habitat and IGAD providing an anticipatory action framework to help city and municipal leaders prepare for El Niño-related risks. The guide outlines practical measures for translating climate forecasts into early action through effective early warning systems, impact-based scenarios, pre-agreed triggers, anticipatory financing, institutional coordination and sector-specific preparedness. It offers actionable guidance for strengthening urban resilience, protecting v',7.0,'classified',NULL,132);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9443,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/cop31-ifrc-calls-urgent-investment-protect-worlds-most-vulnerable','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/cop31-ifrc-calls-urgent-investment-protect-worlds-most-vulnerable','COP31: IFRC calls for urgent investment to protect world''s most vulnerable','cop31ifrccallsforurgentinvestmenttoprotectworldsmostvulnerable','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-04T09:33:06Z','2026-11-05T04:11:19Z','Country: World Source: International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies Geneva, 4 November 2026 - The International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC) is calling on world leaders gathering at COP31 to urgently scale up investment to better protect communities from the growing humanitarian impacts of climate change. Across the world, extreme heat, floods, droughts and storms are threatening lives, livelihoods and health, with the greatest impacts often falling on communities already facing poverty, conflict and displacement. With a stronger El Niño expecte',2.0,'classified',NULL,279);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9444,'https://reliefweb.int/report/chile/chl-ola-de-calor-11-2026-alerta-temprana-preventiva-ola-de-calor-2026-11-05','https://reliefweb.int/report/chile/chl-ola-de-calor-11-2026-alerta-temprana-preventiva-ola-de-calor-2026-11-05','Chile: CHL: Ola de calor - 11-2026 - Alerta Temprana Preventiva Ola de Calor (2026-11-05)','chilechloladecalor112026alertatempranapreventivaoladecalor20261105','reliefweb_ew_es','ReliefWeb - Updates','es','2026-11-05T00:32:40Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','Country: Chile Sources: Cruz Roja Chilena, International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies Please refer to the attached file. Fuentes para datos marcados como Otros Servicio Nacional de Prevencion de Respuesta Ante Desastres - SENAPRED Direccion Meteorologica de Chile - DMC Corporacion Nacional Forestal - CONAF Descripción RESUMEN DE LA SITUACIÓN De acuerdo a los compromisos adquiridos en la Ley Marco de Cambio Climático Nº 21.455 del Ministerio del Medio Ambiente y al Anexo del Plan Nacional de Emergencias ante la amenaza de calor extremo, se prevén eventos de calor durante e',5.0,'classified',NULL,248);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9445,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/cop31-la-ifrc-llama-invertir-urgentemente-para-proteger-las-personas-mas-vulnerables-del-mundo','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/cop31-la-ifrc-llama-invertir-urgentemente-para-proteger-las-personas-mas-vulnerables-del-mundo','World: COP31: La IFRC llama a invertir urgentemente para proteger a las personas más vulnerables del mundo','worldcop31laifrcllamaainvertirurgentementeparaprotegeralaspersonasmasvulnerablesdelmundo','reliefweb_ew_es','ReliefWeb - Updates','es','2026-11-04T20:03:05Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','Country: World Source: International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies Ginebra, 4 de noviembre de 2026 - La Federación Internacional de Sociedades de la Cruz Roja y de la Media Luna Roja (IFRC) hace un llamado a los líderes mundiales reunidos en la COP31 para que aumenten urgentemente la inversión con el fin de proteger mejor a las comunidades de los crecientes efectos humanitarios del cambio climático. En todo el mundo, las olas de calor extremo, las inundaciones, las sequías y las tormentas amenazan las vidas, los medios de subsistencia y la salud, y los efectos más graves s',2.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9446,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/higher-ground-lessons-hurricane-melissa-resilience-relief','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/higher-ground-lessons-hurricane-melissa-resilience-relief','Higher ground: Lessons from Hurricane Melissa for resilience, relief, and recovery','highergroundlessonsfromhurricanemelissaforresiliencereliefandrecovery','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T18:00:05Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','This report assesses Jamaica’s resilience to Hurricane Melissa, finding storm standards, power failures and reactive relief weakened preparedness, despite insurance payouts. It calls for stronger infrastructure, service continuity and finance reform.',2.0,'classified',NULL,286);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9447,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/social-protection-and-climate-crisis','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/social-protection-and-climate-crisis','Social protection and the climate crisis','socialprotectionandtheclimatecrisis','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T17:59:47Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','This guidance note helps governments strengthen climate-responsive social protection, outlining how climate change compounds poverty and vulnerability and actions on evidence, policy, institutions and programme design to address climate risks.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9448,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/concurrent-extreme-heat-and-power-outages-health-impacts','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/concurrent-extreme-heat-and-power-outages-health-impacts','Concurrent extreme heat and power outages: Health impacts, exposure assessment, and research priorities','concurrentextremeheatandpoweroutageshealthimpactsexposureassessmentandresearchpriorities','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T17:59:29Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','This scoping review examines health impacts of concurrent extreme heat and power outages, finding mixed evidence, with respiratory admissions and ambulance attendances among outcomes linked to outages; it calls for better monitoring and preparedness.',2.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9449,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/toward-health-aware-urban-flood-resilience-conceptual','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/toward-health-aware-urban-flood-resilience-conceptual','Toward health-aware urban flood resilience: A conceptual framework linking drainage conditions to flood forecasting and control','towardhealthawareurbanfloodresilienceaconceptualframeworklinkingdrainageconditionstofloodforecastingandcontrol','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T17:58:26Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','This commentary proposes a health-aware urban flood resilience framework that feeds drainage condition into forecasting and management. Dajiangou simulations show blockage and sediment can increase peak surface-water depths.',1.0,'classified',NULL,285);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9450,'https://www.preventionweb.net/news/new-framework-global-sea-level-observations','https://preventionweb.net/news/new-framework-global-sea-level-observations','A new framework for global sea-level observations','anewframeworkforglobalsealevelobservations','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T17:55:38Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','A renewed plan, a landmark lecture and recognition at the UN General Assembly: 2026 has been a defining year for the Global Sea Level Observing System.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9451,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/building-resilience-blueprint-what-works-what-doesnt-and-why','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/building-resilience-blueprint-what-works-what-doesnt-and-why','Building resilience into the blueprint: What works, what doesn''t, and why? Insights from Asia-Pacific countries on risk-informed spatial planning','buildingresilienceintotheblueprintwhatworkswhatdoesntandwhyinsightsfromasiapacificcountriesonriskinformedspatialplanning','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T17:55:03Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','This report examines risk-informed spatial planning as a tool for reducing disaster risk, drawing lessons from South Korea, Australia, the Philippines, and China.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9452,'https://www.preventionweb.net/news/when-el-nino-meets-fragility-and-conflict-can-emergency-seed-aid-build-resilience','https://preventionweb.net/news/when-el-nino-meets-fragility-and-conflict-can-emergency-seed-aid-build-resilience','When El Niño meets fragility and conflict: Can emergency seed aid build resilience?','whenelninomeetsfragilityandconflictcanemergencyseedaidbuildresilience','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T17:51:36Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','IFPRI is launching new research on seed systems in conflict zones. The project in northern Ethiopia and northern Nigeria examines how climate shocks, conflict, and displacement affect seed access and local seed systems.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9453,'https://www.preventionweb.net/news/fragile-progress-how-cop31-can-advance-climate-security','https://preventionweb.net/news/fragile-progress-how-cop31-can-advance-climate-security','Fragile progress: How COP31 can advance climate security','fragileprogresshowcop31canadvanceclimatesecurity','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T17:51:02Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','Australia and Türkiye have an opportunity to put climate, peace and security back on the COP31 agenda by integrating conflict sensitivity into climate adaptation, increasing finance for fragile states and turning commitments into action.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9454,'https://www.preventionweb.net/news/undrr-and-japan-showcase-tsunami-innovation-geneva-policy-dialogue','https://preventionweb.net/news/undrr-and-japan-showcase-tsunami-innovation-geneva-policy-dialogue','UNDRR and Japan showcase tsunami innovation at Geneva policy dialogue','undrrandjapanshowcasetsunamiinnovationatgenevapolicydialogue','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T15:57:52Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','To commemorate World Tsunami Awareness Day – marked each year on 5 November – UNDRR held an innovation showcase and policy dialogue, generously hosted by the Permanent Mission of Japan in Geneva.',1.0,'classified',NULL,284);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9455,'https://www.preventionweb.net/organization/caribbean-policy-research-institute','https://preventionweb.net/organization/caribbean-policy-research-institute','Caribbean Policy Research Institute','caribbeanpolicyresearchinstitute','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T15:46:57Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','CAPRI is a not-for profit, public policy think tank dedicated to the production and dissemination of impartial, evidence-based knowledge to inform economic, governance, sustainable and social policy decision-making in Jamaica and the wider Caribbean.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(9456,'https://www.preventionweb.net/organization/transform-0','https://preventionweb.net/organization/transform-0','TRANSFORM','transform','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-11-04T15:29:35Z','2026-11-05T04:11:21Z','TRANSFORM is an innovative capacity development initiative that strengthens individual and institutional capacity and leadership for the implementation of national social protection systems in Africa and the Arab Region.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
