INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(11161,'https://reliefweb.int/report/nepal/unicef-nepal-humanitarian-situation-report-no-8-2-november-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/nepal/unicef-nepal-humanitarian-situation-report-no-8-2-november-2026','UNICEF Nepal Humanitarian Situation Report No. 8, 2 November 2026','unicefnepalhumanitariansituationreportno82november2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-09T04:07:30Z','2026-11-09T04:10:04Z','Country: Nepal Source: UN Children''s Fund Please refer to the attached file. Highlights Children are bearing the brunt of the disaster. More than 32,000 children were affected by the Rasuwa-Bhotekoshi flash floods on 26 August 2026, with many losing loved ones, homes and belongings, and facing heightened risks to their health, education, protection and well-being. Further flash flooding along the Budhi Gandaki River on 11 October affected communities, causing additional damage to infrastructure and access routes. Since the onset of the crisis, UNICEF has worked alongside the Government of Nepa',2.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(11162,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/financing-last-mile-investment-case-early-warnings-all','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/financing-last-mile-investment-case-early-warnings-all','World: Financing the Last Mile: An Investment Case for Early Warnings for All','worldfinancingthelastmileaninvestmentcaseforearlywarningsforall','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-09T03:12:27Z','2026-11-09T04:10:04Z','Country: World Source: International Water Management Institute Please refer to the attached file. Citation Amarnath, Giriraj, Alok Sikka, Ian Overton, Ritu Bharadwaj, Avinash Venkata Adavikolanu, and Catalina Jamie. 2026. Financing the Last Mile: An Investment Case for Early Warnings for All. International Water Management Institute. https://doi.org/10.5337/2026.233 . Abstract/Description With a year to the United Nations’ Early Warnings for All deadline, the case for early warning is settled: countries with comprehensive multi-hazard early warning systems record disaster mortality nearly six',6.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(11163,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/state-early-warning-around-world-november-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/state-early-warning-around-world-november-2026','The State of Early Warning Around the World (November 2026)','thestateofearlywarningaroundtheworldnovember2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-09T03:08:23Z','2026-11-09T04:10:04Z','Country: World Source: International Water Management Institute Please refer to the attached file. Citation Amarnath, Giriraj, and Niranga Alahacoon. 2026. The State of Early Warning Around the World. International Water Management Institute (IWMI). https://doi.org/10.5337/2026.232 . Abstract/Description The United Nations’ Early Warnings for All (EW4All) initiative set 2027 as the year by which everyone on Earth should be protected by a multi-hazard early warning system. This report takes stock of progress towards that goal, drawing on the Eyes on the Storm webinar series convened by the Inte',8.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(11164,'https://reliefweb.int/report/angola/angola-food-security-outlook-october-2026-may-2027-below-average-2026-harvest-driving-crisis-aligned-outcomes-southern-angola','https://reliefweb.int/report/angola/angola-food-security-outlook-october-2026-may-2027-below-average-2026-harvest-driving-crisis-aligned-outcomes-southern-angola','Angola Food Security Outlook October 2026 - May 2027: Below-average 2026 harvest is driving Crisis-aligned outcomes in southern Angola','angolafoodsecurityoutlookoctober2026may2027belowaverage2026harvestisdrivingcrisisalignedoutcomesinsouthernangola','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-09T01:38:27Z','2026-11-09T04:10:04Z','Country: Angola Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages Crisis (IPC Phase 3)-aligned outcomes are expected across Benguela, Namibe, Cunene, southern Huila, and Cuando Cubango provinces from October 2026 to January 2027 . Household food stocks have depleted following below-average harvests, increasing dependence on market purchases amid high food prices. Limited income-earning opportunities and reduced purchasing power are constraining access to food, resulting in food consumption gaps. Poor households are reducing meal size and frequency, int',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(11165,'https://reliefweb.int/report/lesotho/lesotho-food-security-outlook-october-2026-may-2027-depleted-stocks-and-below-average-harvest-sustain-stressed-outcomes','https://reliefweb.int/report/lesotho/lesotho-food-security-outlook-october-2026-may-2027-depleted-stocks-and-below-average-harvest-sustain-stressed-outcomes','Lesotho Food Security Outlook October 2026 - May 2027: Depleted stocks and below-average harvest to sustain Stressed outcomes','lesothofoodsecurityoutlookoctober2026may2027depletedstocksandbelowaverageharvesttosustainstressedoutcomes','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-09T01:35:57Z','2026-11-09T04:10:04Z','Country: Lesotho Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages Stressed (IPC Phase 2) outcomes are expected to persist across the Southern Lowlands, Senqu River Valley, and Mountains through May 2027 , with an increasing number of poor households facing Crisis (IPC Phase 3) during the December to February lean season. Having depleted their own-produced stocks from the below-average 2026 harvest atypically early, poor households are market reliant ahead of the lean season, while below-average income from self-employment, agricultural labor, and remi',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(11166,'https://reliefweb.int/report/madagascar/madagascar-food-security-outlook-prolonged-crisis-expected-across-grand-south-recovery-202526-lags-october-2026-may-2027','https://reliefweb.int/report/madagascar/madagascar-food-security-outlook-prolonged-crisis-expected-across-grand-south-recovery-202526-lags-october-2026-may-2027','Madagascar - Food Security Outlook: Prolonged Crisis expected across the Grand South as recovery from 2025/26 lags, October 2026 - May 2027','madagascarfoodsecurityoutlookprolongedcrisisexpectedacrossthegrandsouthasrecoveryfrom202526lagsoctober2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-11-09T01:26:53Z','2026-11-09T04:10:04Z','Country: Madagascar Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages Crisis (IPC Phase 3) outcomes are expected to persist across the Grand South through May 2027, as poor households face lingering impacts from the poor 2025/26 agricultural season, including depleted food stocks, high indebtedness, and weakened livelihoods. Below-average rainfall, limited seed access, and reduced agricultural labor opportunities will continue to constrain food production, incomes, and household purchasing power, and stall livelihood recovery. Below-average harvests ar',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
