ent against intense rains in Huarochirí province", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(108,'','tropical_cyclone','2026-10-22T03:23:41Z','2026-10-22T03:09:51Z','2026-10-19','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs", "type": "international"}, {"country": null, "name": "United Nations Development Programme", "type": "international"}], "agency_types": ["international"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "HT", "name": "Haiti"}], "event_date": "2026-10-19", "event_location": "Haiti", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-10-22T03:09:51Z", "hazard": "tropical_cyclone", "hazards": ["tropical_cyclone"], "id": 108, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["fr"], "last_updated": "2026-10-22T03:09:51Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes an anticipatory action framework for hurricane season but reports no specific event outcome.", "pillars": [1, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-19T20:46:06Z", "source_name": "ReliefWeb - Updates", "title": "Haiti: Cadre d’Action Anticipatoire : Tempêtes/Ouragans en Haïti (2026)", "title_en": "Haiti: Anticipatory Action Framework: Storms/Hurricanes in Haiti (2026)", "url": "https://reliefweb.int/report/haiti/cadre-daction-anticipatoire-tempetesouragans-en-haiti-2026"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "An OCHA document presents an anticipatory action framework for storms and hurricanes in Haiti for 2026. It highlights that 96% of the population is exposed to climate risks, including intensifying cyclonic systems, during the Atlantic hurricane season. The framework addresses risk knowledge and preparedness for early action.", "title": "Haiti: Anticipatory Action Framework: Storms/Hurricanes in Haiti (2026)", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(109,'other|ET|ethiopia and south africa','other','2026-10-22T03:23:42Z','2026-10-24T03:04:57Z','2026-10-20','{"actions": ["protective action taken by community members after receiving early warning messages"], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": ["other"], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "ET", "name": "Ethiopia"}, {"code": "ZA", "name": "South Africa"}], "event_date": "2026-10-20", "event_location": "Ethiopia and South Africa", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-10-22T03:09:53Z", "hazard": "other", "hazards": ["other"], "id": 109, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-10-24T03:04:57Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "mixed", "outcome_justification": "Study finds direct recipients reported more complete warnings and were more likely to take protective action than those receiving information indirectly, indicating uneven effectiveness of warning reception.", "pillars": [3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-20T14:29:18Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Associations between early warning message completeness, reception mode, and protective action across four at-risk communities in Ethiopia and South Africa", "title_en": "Associations between early warning message completeness, reception mode, and protective action across four at-risk communities in Ethiopia and South Africa", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/associations-between-early-warning-message-completeness"}, {"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-23T13:35:09Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Hazard impact information has the greatest effect on how people respond to alerts", "title_en": "Hazard impact information has the greatest effect on how people respond to alerts", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/news/hazard-impact-information-has-greatest-effect-how-people-respond-alerts"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A study across four at-risk communities in Ethiopia and South Africa examines the completeness of early warning messages and how they were received. It finds that people receiving warnings directly reported more complete messages and were more likely to take protective action than those receiving information indirectly. The findings highlight the importance of direct, complete warning dissemination for effective protective response.", "title": "Associations between early warning message completeness, reception mode, and protective action across four at-risk communities in Ethiopia and South Africa", "wmo_regions": ["I"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(110,'earthquake|US|california','earthquake','2026-10-22T03:23:42Z','2026-10-22T03:09:53Z','2026-10-20','{"actions": [], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.6, "countries": [{"code": "US", "name": "United States"}], "event_date": "2026-10-20", "event_location": "California, USA", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-10-22T03:09:53Z", "hazard": "earthquake", "hazards": ["earthquake"], "id": 110, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-10-22T03:09:53Z", "lead_time": "up to one day (forecast horizon)", "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item reports research showing earthquake forecasting models can reliably describe short-term activity patterns, but no warnings issued or actions taken are described.", "pillars": [2], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-20T14:53:51Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Forecasting research could help millions living in earthquake-prone regions", "title_en": "Forecasting research could help millions living in earthquake-prone regions", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/news/forecasting-research-could-help-millions-living-earthquake-prone-regions"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A decade-long study of earthquake activity in California provides the strongest evidence to date that forecasting models can reliably describe earthquake activity patterns over the following day. The research suggests such forecasts could help people in earthquake-prone regions. Its relevance to early warning is in the detection and forecasting pillar, though no operational warning service is described.", "title": "Forecasting research could help millions living in earthquake-prone regions", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(111,'named|20 black summer bushfires','wildfire','2026-10-22T03:23:42Z','2026-10-22T03:09:53Z','2026-10-20','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": "AU", "name": "NSW Rural Fire Service", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.6, "countries": [{"code": "AU", "name": "Australia"}], "event_date": "2026-10-20", "event_location": "New South Wales, Australia", "event_name": "2019–20 Black Summer bushfires", "first_seen": "2026-10-22T03:09:53Z", "hazard": "wildfire", "hazards": ["wildfire"], "id": 111, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-10-22T03:09:53Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet analyses risk mapping and house losses but does not report whether warnings were issued or acted upon during the event.", "pillars": [1], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-20T14:54:40Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "House loss patterns in the Australian 2019–20 fire disaster confirm the reliability of official risk mapping", "title_en": "House loss patterns in the Australian 2019–20 fire disaster confirm the reliability of official risk mapping", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/house-loss-patterns-australian-2019-20-fire-disaster-confirm"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A study of 2019–20 New South Wales wildfire losses found 94% of destroyed houses lay within 100 m of mapped flammable vegetation, supporting the validity of the NSW Bush Fire Prone Land mapping buffer. The authors note that risk extends further under extreme fire weather. The item concerns risk knowledge (pillar 1) rather than real-time warning delivery.", "title": "House loss patterns in the Australian 2019–20 fire disaster confirm the reliability of official risk mapping", "wmo_regions": ["V"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(112,'flood|JP|akita prefecture','flood','2026-10-22T03:23:42Z','2026-10-24T03:13:38Z','2026-10-20','{"actions": ["Issuance of a Level 5 flood special warning (氾濫特別警報) for the Kohoyoshi River via JMA press release", "Level 5 flood emergency special warning issued for Kohoku River", "Advice to avoid moving in the dark and not to evacuate recklessly; move to upper floors instead", "Advice to avoid using cars in flood-risk areas", "Residents urged to ensure their personal safety", "Residents urged to take immediate life-protecting action", "JMA and MLIT held emergency press conference", "Special flood warning (level 5 flood emergency warning) issued for Kozukawa river in Akita Prefecture"], "agencies": [{"country": "JP", "name": "Japan Meteorological Agency", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Japan Meteorological Agency (JMA)", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Japan Weather Association", "type": "media"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Kyodo News", "type": "media"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Nippon TV NEWS NNN", "type": "media"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "TBS NEWS DIG", "type": "media"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Akita Prefectural Government", "type": "other_national_agency"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Akita Prefectural Police", "type": "other_national_agency"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism (MLIT)", "type": "other_national_agency"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Yurihonjo City", "type": "other_national_agency"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Yurihonjo City Fire Department", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS", "media", "other_national_agency"], "channels": ["other", "tv", "website"], "confidence": 0.97, "countries": [{"code": "JP", "name": "Japan"}], "event_date": "2026-10-20", "event_location": "Akita Prefecture, Japan", "event_name": "Typhoon Hagibis-type event (typhoon No. 30, 2026)", "first_seen": "2026-10-22T03:10:58Z", "hazard": "flood", "hazards": ["flash_flood", "flood"], "id": 112, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["ja"], "last_updated": "2026-10-24T03:13:38Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "negative", "outcome_justification": "The item is an official JMA press release announcing the warning; no information on public response, damage or lives saved is given.", "pillars": [2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-20T15:00:00Z", "source_name": "気象庁 (JMA)", "title": "子吉川（秋田県）にレベル５氾濫特別警報発表", "title_en": "Level 5 flood special warning issued for the Kohoyoshi River (Akita Prefecture)", "url": "https://www.jma.go.jp/jma/press/2610/21b/20261021_hanran_tokukei.html"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T00:05:00Z", "source_name": "NHK ニュース 主要", "title": "秋田 子吉川に一時氾濫特別警報 川の増水など注意を", "title_en": "Akita: Special flood warning issued for Kohoku River; caution against rising rivers", "url": "https://news.web.nhk/newsweb/na/nd-20261021de63227"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T01:58:17Z", "source_name": "朝日新聞 (Asahi Shimbun)", "title": "秋田の河原で80代男性発見、心肺停止 子吉川で一時氾濫特別警報", "title_en": "80-something man found in cardiac arrest on riverbank of Akita''s Koyoshi River amid level 5 flood special warning", "url": "http://www.asahi.com/articles/ASVBQ0HRZVBQOXIE004M.html?ref=rss"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T03:13:33Z", "source_name": "news.yahoo.co.jp", "title": "「暗い中の移動は危険 無理な避難せず上の階へ」気象庁 浸水リスク地域で車を利用しないよう呼びかけ 秋田県・子吉川に「レベル5氾濫特別警報」（TBS NEWS DIG Powered by JNN） - Yahoo!ニュース", "title_en": "\"Dangerous to move in the dark; do not evacuate recklessly, move to upper floors\" JMA calls for avoiding car use in flood-risk areas; Level 5 Flood Emergency Special Warning issued for Kohoku River, Akita Prefecture (TBS NEWS DIG)", "url": "https://news.yahoo.co.jp/articles/5e95b469c973ada3476fec864b1e7b6c109601a9"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T03:15:03Z", "source_name": "tenki.jp", "title": "雨雲レーダー(実況) / リアルタイムの雨雲 - 日本気象協会 tenki.jp", "title_en": "Real-time rain cloud radar - Japan Weather Association tenki.jp", "url": "https://tenki.jp/radar/"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T03:15:03Z", "source_name": "news.yahoo.co.jp", "title": "秋田の子吉川に氾濫特別警報 レベル5、気象庁（共同通信） - Yahoo!ニュース", "title_en": "Level 5 flood emergency warning issued for Akita''s Koyoshi River by Japan Meteorological Agency (Kyodo News)", "url": "https://news.yahoo.co.jp/articles/8c03534e6142ed53f96a5394797469eb1c5695bf"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T03:15:03Z", "source_name": "okinawatimes.co.jp", "title": "秋田県の河川にレベル５氾濫特別警報", "title_en": "Level 5 flood special warning issued for rivers in Akita Prefecture", "url": "https://okinawatimes.co.jp/articles/-/1949564"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T03:15:03Z", "source_name": "sanin-chuo.co.jp", "title": "氾濫特別警報を注意報に切り替え", "title_en": "Flood special warning downgraded to flood advisory", "url": "https://sanin-chuo.co.jp/articles/-/1101885"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T03:18:55Z", "source_name": "news.infoseek.co.jp", "title": "秋田・子吉川にレベル5「氾濫特別警報」｜Infoseekニュース", "title_en": "Level 5 \"flood emergency special warning\" issued for Kokai River in Akita", "url": "https://news.infoseek.co.jp/article/ntv_2026102105147535"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-22T03:18:55Z", "source_name": "news.yahoo.co.jp", "title": "気象庁と国交省が緊急会見 秋田で記録的大雨「警報級が続く可能性高い」“原因の1つ”に台風30号（日テレNEWS NNN） - Yahoo!ニュース", "title_en": "Japan Meteorological Agency and MLIT hold emergency press conference; record heavy rain in Akita, ''warning-level conditions likely to continue'', typhoon No. 30 cited as one cause", "url": "https://news.yahoo.co.jp/articles/0fafc9d1445d42da15f69287faf46636dea4dfd0"}], "summaries_original": {"ja": "気象庁が子吉川（秋田県）に氾濫特別警報（レベル５）を発表したことを伝える報道発表。"}, "summary_en": "JMA issued a Level 5 flood special warning (the highest flood alert level) for the Kohoyoshi River in Akita Prefecture, as announced in an official press release on 2026-10-21 (published 2026-10-20 UTC). The release concerns a forecast of river flooding threatening life and property. No impact or response details are provided in the snippet.", "title": "Level 5 flood special warning issued for the Kohoyoshi River (Akita Prefecture)", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(113,'flood|JP|hakui city','heavy_rain','2026-10-22T03:23:44Z','2026-10-22T03:10:58Z','2026-10-21','{"actions": ["Issued evacuation advisory (high-risk evacuation for elderly and others, warning level 3) to about 85,000 households / 19,000+ people across the whole city after a level 3 heavy rain warning was issued"], "agencies": [{"country": "JP", "name": "Japan Meteorological Agency", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Hakui City government", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS", "other_national_agency"], "channels": ["other"], "confidence": 0.95, "countries": [{"code": "JP", "name": "Japan"}], "event_date": "2026-10-21", "event_location": "Hakui City, Ishikawa Prefecture, Japan", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-10-22T03:10:58Z", "hazard": "heavy_rain", "hazards": ["heavy_rain"], "id": 113, "impacts": {"people_reached": 19000}, "languages": ["ja"], "last_updated": "2026-10-22T03:10:58Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports the advisory being issued but gives no information on its effects or on whether residents evacuated.", "pillars": [3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-10-21T09:42:16Z", "source_name": "NHK ニュース 社会", "title": "石川 羽咋市 高齢者等避難の情報", "title_en": "Hakui City, Ishikawa: Evacuation advisory for elderly and others issued", "url": "https://news.web.nhk/newsweb/na/nd-20261021de63091"}], "summaries_original": {"ja": "石川県羽咋市は、市内にレベル3大雨警報が発表されたことを受け、21日午後6時、市内全域のおよそ8500世帯1万9000人あまりに、高齢者等避難の情報を出しました。5段階の警戒レベルのうちレベル3に相当します。"}, "summary_en": "Hakui City in Ishikawa Prefecture issued a high-risk evacuation advisory for the elderly and others covering the whole city, roughly 8,500 households and over 19,000 people, at 6 p.m. on 21 October after a level 3 heavy rain warning was issued for the city. The advisory corresponds to warning level 3 on Japan''s five-level alert scale. The snippet does not report outcomes.", "title": "Hakui City, Ishikawa: Evacuation advisory for elderly and others issued", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(114,'','other','2026-10-22T03:23:45Z','2026-10-22T03:10:43Z','2026-10-21','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": "GB", "name": "Met Office", "type": "NMHS"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.2, "countries": [{"code": "GB", "name": "United Kingdom"}], "event_date": "2026-10-21", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-10-22T03:10:43Z", "hazard": "other", "hazards": ["other"], "id": 114, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-10-22T03:10:43Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes a Met Office warning about power cuts, which is not a natural hazard warning; the nature of the warning is unclear from the snippet alone.", "pillars": [], "review": true, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-10-21T11:00:00Z", "source_name": "express.co.uk", "title": "Met Office issues 7 to 14 - hour power cuts warnings to 65 united kingdom areas on Friday", "title_en": "Met Office issues 7 to 14 - hour power cuts warnings to 65 united kingdom areas on Friday", "url": "https://www.express.co.uk/news/weather/2259113/met-office-issues-7-14hour"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "The Met Office reportedly warned that power cuts could affect as many as 65 UK areas on Friday, with outages of 7 to 14 hours. The snippet does not indicate a natural hazard, so the item appears outside the scope of natural-hazard early warning monitoring.", "title": "Met Office issues 7 to 14 - hour power cuts warnings to 65 united kingdom areas on Friday", "wmo_regions": ["VI"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(115,'multi_hazard|AR|mendoza','multi_hazard','2026-10-22T03:23:45Z','2026-10-22T03:19:53Z','2026-10-21','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": "AR", "name": "Servicio Meteorológico Nacional", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "AR", "name": "Clarín", "type": "media"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS", "media"], "channels": ["other"], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "AR", "name": "Argentina"}], "event_date": "2026-10-21", "event_location": "Mendoza, Argentina", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-10-22T03:19:53Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 115, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-10-22T03:19:53Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports SMN anticipating a strong or very strong El Niño impact and yellow alerts in several provinces, but gives no information on how warnings were received or acted upon.", "pillars": [2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-10-21T11:48:32Z", "source_name": "Clarín (Argentina) sociedad", "title": "Súper Niño 2026 en Argentina, EN VIVO: qué provincias están bajo alerta por tormentas y dónde habrá lluvias intensas", "title_en": "Super El Niño 2026 in Argentina, LIVE: which provinces are under alert for storms and where heavy rains will fall", "url": "https://www.clarin.com/sociedad/super-nino-2026-argentina-vivo-ciudades-riesgo-inundacion-llega-pico-crecida_0_Dj4pnOq6Lc.html"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "El Servicio Meteorológico Nacional anticipó que el fenómeno alcanzará en el centro-este argentino una intensidad fuerte o muy fuerte. Una tormenta con granizo azotó Mendoza y varias provincias están bajo alerta amarilla."}, "summary_en": "Argentina''s National Meteorological Service (SMN) anticipated that the 2026 El Niño phenomenon would reach strong or very strong intensity in central-eastern Argentina. A hailstorm hit Mendoza and several provinces were placed 