PAACT Program reports that El Niño is established and expected to strengthen, with WMO forecasts showing near-100% likelihood it persists through February 2028 and a high chance of becoming very strong. It references the recently released GHACOF-74 forecast for the Greater Horn of Africa, covering Djibouti, Ethiopia and Somalia. The update focuses on forecast-based preparedness for the region.", "title": "World: El Niño Preparedness & Response Situation Update - Issued by IMPAACT Program, Issue No. 1 (October 2026)", "wmo_regions": ["I", "II", "III", "IV", "V", "VI"]}');
