 and critical points in Tumbes region", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(294,'flood|PE|sierra sur','heavy_rain','2026-11-06T04:15:32Z','2026-11-07T04:15:48Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["INDECI recommends preparedness measures in response to SENAMHI meteorological warning No. 455 (orange level)", "INDECI recommends preparedness measures in response to SENAMHI meteorological warning No. 456 (red level)"], "agencies": [{"country": "PE", "name": "SENAMHI", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "PE", "name": "INDECI", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS", "other_national_agency"], "channels": ["website"], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [{"code": "PE", "name": "Peru"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Sierra sur, Peru", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:13:49Z", "hazard": "heavy_rain", "hazards": ["heavy_rain"], "id": 294, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:15:48Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes a warning and recommended preparedness measures but does not report any outcome.", "pillars": [3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": null, "source_name": "INDECI Perú noticias", "title": "INDECI recomienda medidas de preparación ante precipitaciones en la sierra sur", "title_en": "INDECI recommends preparedness measures for precipitation in the southern highlands", "url": "https://www.gob.pe/institucion/indeci/noticias/1470092-indeci-recomienda-medidas-de-preparacion-ante-precipitaciones-en-la-sierra-sur"}, {"language": "es", "published_at": null, "source_name": "INDECI Perú noticias", "title": "INDECI recomienda medidas de preparación ante precipitaciones en la costa y sierra", "title_en": "INDECI recommends preparedness measures for precipitation in the coast and highlands", "url": "https://www.gob.pe/institucion/indeci/noticias/1470584-indeci-recomienda-medidas-de-preparacion-ante-precipitaciones-en-la-costa-y-sierra"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "INDECI recomienda medidas de preparación ante el aviso meteorológico N.° 455 (nivel naranja) del SENAMHI, por precipitaciones (nieve, granizo, aguanieve y lluvia) en la sierra sur del país."}, "summary_en": "INDECI issued a press release recommending preparedness measures for snow, hail, sleet and rain in the southern highlands of Peru, following SENAMHI meteorological warning No. 455 at orange level. The item centres on the dissemination of a SENAMHI warning and the response guidance that followed. No outcome is reported in the snippet.", "title": "INDECI recommends preparedness measures for precipitation in the southern highlands", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(295,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-06T04:15:33Z','2026-11-06T04:13:39Z','2026-11-04','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": "CO", "name": "Ideam", "type": "NMHS"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS"], "channels": ["website"], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [{"code": "CO", "name": "Colombia"}], "event_date": "2026-11-04", "event_location": "Colombia", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:13:39Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 295, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:13:39Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports ongoing alert status and forecasts but no outcomes of the warnings.", "pillars": [2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-04T04:13:31Z", "source_name": "infobae.com", "title": "Ideam prevé lluvias y mantiene alertas por crecientes súbitas y deslizamientos en Colombia hoy 3 de noviembre: consulte el pronóstico del clima - Infobae", "title_en": "Ideam forecasts rain and maintains alerts for flash floods and landslides in Colombia today, 3 November: check the weather forecast", "url": "https://www.infobae.com/colombia/2026/11/03/ideam-preve-lluvias-y-mantiene-alertas-por-crecientes-subitas-y-deslizamientos-en-colombia-hoy-3-de-noviembre-consulte-el-pronostico-del-clima/"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "El Ideam informó que 196 subzonas hidrográficas y 429 municipios permanecen bajo algún nivel de alerta por crecientes súbitas, inundaciones o movimientos en masa, con una subzona en alerta roja en el área Magdalena-Cauca."}, "summary_en": "Ideam reports that 196 hydrographic subzones and 429 municipalities remain under some level of alert for flash floods, floods or mass movements, including one subzone under red alert in the Magdalena-Cauca area. The item covers ongoing rain forecasts and alert maintenance by Colombia''s national meteorological service.", "title": "Ideam forecasts rain and maintains alerts for flash floods and landslides in Colombia today, 3 November: check the weather forecast", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(296,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-06T04:15:33Z','2026-11-06T04:11:16Z','2026-11-04','{"actions": ["Implementation of the Rapid Refresh Forecast System (RRFS), a next-generation rapid-update numerical forecast system"], "agencies": [{"country": "US", "name": "NOAA", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "US", "name": "National Weather Service", "type": "NMHS"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS"], "channels": ["website"], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "US", "name": "United States"}], "event_date": "2026-11-04", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:11:16Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 296, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:11:16Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes the launch of an improved forecasting system intended to deliver earlier, more accurate forecasts; no outcomes of warnings are reported.", "pillars": [2], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-04T20:22:45Z", "source_name": "NOAA / US National Weather Service news", "title": "NOAA weather modeling hits key milestone with Rapid Refresh Forecast System debut", "title_en": "NOAA weather modeling hits key milestone with Rapid Refresh Forecast System debut", "url": "https://www.noaa.gov/news-release/noaa-weather-modeling-hits-key-milestone-with-rapid-refresh-forecast-system-debut"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "NOAA implemented its next-generation Rapid Refresh Forecast System (RRFS) on November 3, a rapid-update numerical weather model intended to deliver earlier and more accurate forecasts to support protection of life and property. The item concerns detection, monitoring and forecasting capability (EW4All pillar 2) rather than a specific hazard event.", "title": "NOAA weather modeling hits key milestone with Rapid Refresh Forecast System debut", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(297,'multi_hazard|BT|himalayas','multi_hazard','2026-11-06T04:15:33Z','2026-11-06T04:07:04Z','2026-11-04','{"actions": [], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "BT", "name": "Bhutan"}, {"code": "CN", "name": "China"}, {"code": "IN", "name": "India"}, {"code": "NP", "name": "Nepal"}, {"code": "PK", "name": "Pakistan"}], "event_date": "2026-11-04", "event_location": "Himalayas", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:07:04Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 297, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:07:04Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item is a research paper proposing a cascade-aware approach to early warning; it does not report outcomes of specific warnings.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-04T22:18:56Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Rethinking cascading high-mountain hazards and early warning in the Himalayas", "title_en": "Rethinking cascading high-mountain hazards and early warning in the Himalayas", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/rethinking-cascading-high-mountain-hazards-and-early-warning"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A publication argues for a four-tier cascade-aware approach to high-mountain hazards in the Himalayas, spanning source-zone monitoring, failure detection, early warning, and preparedness, planning and governance. It addresses how cascading hazards such as glacial and landslide chains can be better detected and warned for. The item is a policy/research framing rather than a report on a specific warning event.", "title": "Rethinking cascading high-mountain hazards and early warning in the Himalayas", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(298,'flood|US|platte county','flood','2026-11-06T04:15:34Z','2026-11-07T04:10:42Z','2026-11-05','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": "US", "name": "National Weather Service Kansas City/Pleasant Hill", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "US", "name": "KQ2", "type": "media"}, {"country": "US", "name": "NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS", "media", "other_national_agency"], "channels": ["other", "website"], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "US", "name": "United States"}], "event_date": "2026-11-05", "event_location": "Platte County, Missouri, USA", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:11:15Z", "hazard": "flood", "hazards": ["flood"], "id": 298, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:10:42Z", "lead_time": "until November 8, 2026 at 7:32PM CST (warning period)", "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item reports a forecast flood warning and crest level but no subsequent impacts, actions or outcomes.", "pillars": [2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-05T04:11:11Z", "source_name": "kq2.com", "title": "Flood Warning issued November 4 at 9:58AM CST until November 8 at 7:32PM CST by NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO - KQ2", "title_en": "Flood Warning issued November 4 at 9:58AM CST until November 8 at 7:32PM CST by NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO", "url": "https://www.kq2.com/weather/weather-alerts/2026/11/04/flood-warning-issued-november-4-at-958am-cst-until-november-8-at-732pm-cst-by-nws-kansas-city-pleasant-hill-mo/"}, {"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-07T04:10:38Z", "source_name": "kq2.com", "title": "Flood Warning issued November 6 at 9:27AM CST until November 6 at 6:00PM CST by NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO - KQ2", "title_en": "Flood Warning issued November 6 at 9:27AM CST until November 6 at 6:00PM CST by NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO", "url": "https://www.kq2.com/weather/weather-alerts/2026/11/06/flood-warning-issued-november-6-at-927am-cst-until-november-6-at-600pm-cst-by-nws-kansas-city-pleasant-hill-mo/"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "The National Weather Service Kansas City/Pleasant Hill issued a flood warning for the Platte River in Platte County, Missouri, forecasting minor flooding with a crest of 23.1 feet on Saturday morning. Cropland near Platte City is expected to begin flooding at 20.0 feet. The warning is in effect from November 4 to November 8, 2026.", "title": "Flood Warning issued November 4 at 9:58AM CST until November 8 at 7:32PM CST by NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(299,'multi_hazard|BB|barbados and belize','multi_hazard','2026-11-06T04:15:34Z','2026-11-06T04:07:03Z','2026-11-05','{"actions": ["Forecast-based anticipatory action pilots with Red Cross and Red Crescent National Societies"], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies", "type": "international"}], "agency_types": ["international"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "BB", "name": "Barbados"}, {"code": "BZ", "name": "Belize"}], "event_date": "2026-11-05", "event_location": "Barbados and Belize", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:07:03Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 299, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:07:03Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes the evolution of IFRC forecast-based anticipatory action programmes but reports no specific outcomes.", "pillars": [2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-05T07:33:08Z", "source_name": "ReliefWeb - Updates", "title": "Acting ahead of the storm: How the IFRC is redefining anticipatory action for small states in Barbados and Belize", "title_en": "Acting ahead of the storm: How the IFRC is redefining anticipatory action for small states in Barbados and Belize", "url": "https://reliefweb.int/report/barbados/acting-ahead-storm-how-ifrc-redefining-anticipatory-action-small-states-barbados-and-belize"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "The IFRC describes its evolution of forecast-based and anticipatory action since 2014, formally launched as Forecast-based Action by the IFRC-DREF in 2018 and integrated into the IFRC Strategy 2030. The article focuses on applying anticipatory approaches in small states Barbados and Belize, using forecasts to act ahead of storms. Specific warning outcomes are not given in the snippet.", "title": "Acting ahead of the storm: How the IFRC is redefining anticipatory action for small states in Barbados and Belize", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(300,'other|XX|southern asean region','other','2026-11-06T04:15:35Z','2026-11-06T04:11:21Z','2026-11-05','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "ASEAN Specialised Meteorological Centre (ASMC)", "type": "RSMC"}], "agency_types": ["RSMC"], "channels": ["website"], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [], "event_date": "2026-11-05", "event_location": "Southern ASEAN region", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:11:21Z", "hazard": "other", "hazards": ["other"], "id": 300, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:11:21Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The alert downgrade reports improved haze conditions with low hotspot counts, but no warning impacts or actions are described in the snippet.", "pillars": [2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-05T08:55:23Z", "source_name": "ASEAN Specialised Meteorological Centre", "title": "Alert20261105 – Downgrade to Alert Level 1 for Southern ASEAN Region", "title_en": "Alert20261105 – Downgrade to Alert Level 1 for Southern ASEAN Region", "url": "https://asmc.asean.org/alert20261105-downgrade-to-alert-level-1-for-southern-asean-region/"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "The ASEAN Specialised Meteorological Centre downgraded its transboundary haze alert to Alert Level 1 for the Southern ASEAN region, citing showers that kept hotspot counts low and improved smoke haze conditions. It notes isolated hotspots and localised smoke plumes may still occur over drier areas, though transboundary haze risk is likely reduced. This is a monitoring and alert-level advisory from the regional centre.", "title": "Alert20261105 – Downgrade to Alert Level 1 for Southern ASEAN Region", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(301,'','tsunami','2026-11-06T04:15:35Z','2026-11-06T04:07:04Z','2026-11-05','{"actions": ["Learn route to high ground", "Identify people needing assistance and co-plan support with them"], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.7, "countries": [], "event_date": "2026-11-05", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:07:04Z", "hazard": "tsunami", "hazards": ["tsunami"], "id": 301, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:07:04Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item is an advocacy piece on inclusive tsunami preparedness and reports no specific warning event outcome.", "pillars": [3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-05T10:51:06Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Inclusive tsunami preparedness: Why the people most at risk must help shape the plan", "title_en": "Inclusive tsunami preparedness: Why the people most at risk must help shape the plan", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/drr-community-voices/inclusive-tsunami-preparedness-why-people-most-risk-must-help-shape-plan"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A PreventionWeb community voices piece calls for inclusive tsunami preparedness, urging residents to learn evacuation routes to high ground and to co-plan evacuation support with people who may need assistance. It focuses on preparedness and response for tsunami early warning rather than a specific warning event.", "title": "Inclusive tsunami preparedness: Why the people most at risk must help shape the plan", "wmo_regions": []}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(302,'flood|PE|lima metropolitana','heavy_rain','2026-11-06T04:15:37Z','2026-11-06T04:13:52Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Instructed schools to adopt preventive measures", "Instructed schools to assess emergency risks and safety conditions in public schools"], "agencies": [{"country": "PE", "name": "DRELM (Dirección Regional de Educación de Lima Metropolitana)", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "PE", "name": "Peru"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Lima Metropolitana, Peru", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:13:52Z", "hazard": "heavy_rain", "hazards": ["heavy_rain"], "id": 302, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:13:52Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports alerts and instructions to schools but does not state any outcome of the warnings.", "pillars": [4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-06T00:26:26Z", "source_name": "La República (Perú) sociedad", "title": "¿Habrá clases virtuales por lluvias en Lima? DRELM pide evaluar condiciones de seguridad en colegios públicos ante riesgo de inundaciones", "title_en": "Will there be virtual classes due to rain in Lima? DRELM asks to assess safety conditions in public schools given flood risk", "url": "https://larepublica.pe/sociedad/2026/11/05/habra-clases-virtuales-por-lluvias-en-lima-drelm-pide-evaluar-condiciones-de-seguridad-en-colegios-publicos-ante-riesgo-de-inundaciones-61360"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "Las intensas lluvias en Lima Metropolitana han activado alertas en escuelas públicas. La DRELM instruye a las instituciones a adoptar medidas preventivas y evaluar riesgos de emergencias."}, "summary_en": "Intense rains in Metropolitan Lima activated alerts in public schools, and the regional education directorate (DRELM) instructed institutions to adopt preventive measures and assess emergency risks, including the possibility of virtual classes. The item focuses on school-level preparedness in response to flood risk warnings. No outcome of the alerts is reported in the snippet.", "title": "Will there be virtual classes due to rain in Lima? DRELM asks to assess safety conditions in public schools given flood risk", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(303,'flood|AR|corrientes province','flood','2026-11-06T04:15:37Z','2026-11-06T04:13:31Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Residents calling for materials to reinforce flood defences", "Evacuation of residents from flooded areas in northern Corrientes Province"], "agencies": [{"country": "AR", "name": "UNO Santa Fe", "type": "media"}, {"country": "AR", "name": "Vecinal de Alto Verde (neighbourhood association)", "type": "other"}], "agency_types": ["media", "other"], "channels": ["other"], "confidence": 0.7, "countries": [{"code": "AR", "name": "Argentina"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Alto Verde, Santa Fe, Argentina", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:13:31Z", "hazard": "flood", "hazards": ["flood"], "id": 303, "impacts": {"evacuated": 1967}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:13:31Z", "lead_time": "in the coming days", "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item reports a community warning about imminent road cut-off and isolation, but no official warning outcome is described.", "pillars": [3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-06T00:30:00Z", "source_name": "ellitoral.com.ar", "title": "El Paraná se estaciona y Corrientes tiene 1.967 evacuados por la crecida", "title_en": "The Paraná stabilises and Corrientes has 1,967 evacuees from the flood", "url": "https://www.ellitoral.com.ar/sociedad/2026-11-5-19-39-0-el-parana-se-estaciona-y-corrientes-tiene-1-967-evacuados-por-la-crecida"}, {"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-06T02:00:00Z", "source_name": "unosantafe.com.ar", "title": "Crecida del Paraná: advierten que el acceso a La Boca podría cortarse en los próximos días y más de 1.500 personas podrían quedar aisladas", "title_en": "Paraná river flood: warning that access to La Boca could be cut in the coming days and more than 1,500 people could be isolated", "url": "https://www.unosantafe.com.ar/santa-fe/crecida-del-parana-advierten-que-el-acceso-la-boca-podria-cortarse-los-proximos-dias-y-mas-1500-personas-podrian-quedar-aisladas-n10290690.html"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "El avance del río mantiene en alerta a los vecinos de Alto Verde. El presidente de la vecinal advirtió que el agua está cada vez más cerca del camino y reclamó materiales para reforzar las defensas, ya que su interrupción dejaría aislados a más de 1.500 personas, dos escuelas y un centro de salud."}, "summary_en": "Residents of Alto Verde, along the Paraná river, are on alert as floodwaters approach the access road to La Boca. The neighbourhood association president warned that the road could be cut off in the coming days, isolating more than 1,500 people, two schools and a health centre, and requested materials to reinforce defences.", "title": "Paraná river flood: warning that access to La Boca could be cut in the coming days and more than 1,500 people could be isolated", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(304,'','flood','2026-11-06T04:15:37Z','2026-11-06T04:07:03Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "FEWS NET", "type": "international"}], "agency_types": ["international"], "channels": ["other"], "confidence": 0.6, "countries": [{"code": "KE", "name": "Kenya"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Kenya", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:07:03Z", "hazard": "flood", "hazards": ["flood"], "id": 304, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:07:03Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item is a food security outlook projecting humanitarian food assistance needs; it does not report on warning outcomes, though it is relevant as a forecast of hazard-related impacts.", "pillars": [2], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T00:40:51Z", "source_name": "ReliefWeb - Updates", "title": "Kenya Food Security Outlook Update, October 2026 - May 2027 - Enhanced rains to drive recovery but flood impacts to temporarily sustain Crisis in east", "title_en": "Kenya Food Security Outlook Update, October 2026 - May 2027 - Enhanced rains to drive recovery but flood impacts to temporarily sustain Crisis in east", "url": "https://reliefweb.int/report/kenya/kenya-food-security-outlook-update-october-2026-may-2027-enhanced-rains-drive-recovery-flood-impacts-temporarily-sustain-crisis-east"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "FEWS NET projects that 3.5-4.0 million people in Kenya will require humanitarian food assistance between October 2026 and May 2027, with needs peaking in October-November. Enhanced rains are expected to drive recovery, but flood impacts will temporarily sustain crisis conditions in eastern areas, including refugee settlements and pastoral counties.", "title": "Kenya Food Security Outlook Update, October 2026 - May 2027 - Enhanced rains to drive recovery but flood impacts to temporarily sustain Crisis in east", "wmo_regions": ["I"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(305,'flood|US|mccaysville','flash_flood','2026-11-06T04:15:41Z','2026-11-06T04:13:39Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Town of McCaysville declared a state of emergency", "Evacuations ordered for affected residents", "Rescue operations", "Evacuation orders for residents of specific streets"], "agencies": [{"country": "US", "name": "National Weather Service", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "US", "name": "United States"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "McCaysville, Fannin County, Georgia, USA", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-06T04:13:39Z", "hazard": "flash_flood", "hazards": ["flash_flood"], "id": 305, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-06T04:13:39Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports flash flood warning extension and evacuations but does not state whether warnings were received in time or what the outcome was.", "pillars": [2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-06T04:13:31Z", "source_name": "infobae.com", "title": "Una ciudad de Georgia declara la emergencia por inundaciones y ordena evacuaciones - Infobae", "title_en": "A Georgia city declares emergency over floods and orders evacuations", "url": "https://www.infobae.com/estados-unidos/2026/11/05/una-ciudad-de-georgia-declara-la-emergencia-por-inundaciones-y-ordena-evacuaciones/"}, {"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-06T04:13:31Z", "source_name": "cnnespanol.cnn.com", "title": "Rescates y evacuaciones en curso ante un “evento de inundación catastrófica” en el norte de Georgia y el sur de Tennessee", "title_en": "Rescues and evacuations underway during a \"catastrophic flood event\" in northern Georgia and southern Tennessee", "url": "https://cnnespanol.cnn.com/2026/11/05/clima-y-tiempo/rescates-evacuaciones-inundaciones-georgia-tennessee-trax"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "McCaysville, Georgia, declaró estado de emergencia por inundaciones repentinas que dejaron viviendas anegadas y familias desplazadas, mientras el Servicio Meteorológico Nacional extendió la alerta de inundación repentina en el condado de Fannin."}, "summary_en": "McCaysville, Georgia declared a state of emergency after sudden floods flooded homes and displaced families. The National Weather Service extended its flash flood alert for Fannin County, and evacuations were ordered. The snippet does not detail warning dissemination or lead time.", "title": "A Georgia city declares emergency over floods and orders evacuations", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(306,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-07T04:17:32Z','2026-11-07T04:10:50Z','2026-11-07','{"actions": ["Launch of a national multi-hazard early warning platform in Somalia", "Establishment of a 24/7 situation room"], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "European Union", "type": "international"}, {"country": null, "name": "IGAD Climate Prediction and Applications Centre (ICPAC)", "type": "international"}], "agency_types": ["international"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "SO", "name": "Somalia"}], "event_date": "2026-11-07", "event_location": "Somalia", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:10:50Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 306, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:10:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes the launch of the system and situation room but reports no outcomes of warnings yet.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": null, "source_name": "ICPAC news", "title": "Somalia Switches On Its Multi-Hazard Early Warning System, and a 24/7 Situation Room to Match", "title_en": "Somalia Switches On Its Multi-Hazard Early Warning System, and a 24/7 Situation Room to Match", "url": "https://www.icpac.net/news/somalia-switches-on-its-multi-hazard-early-warning-system-and-a-247-situation-room-to-match/"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "With technical support from ICPAC and funding from the European Union, Somalia has launched a national multi-hazard early warning platform alongside a 24/7 situation room. The initiative strengthens monitoring, forecasting and warning capacity across hazards in Somalia. Operational results were not yet reported in the snippet.", "title": "Somalia Switches On Its Multi-Hazard Early Warning System, and a 24/7 Situation Room to Match", "wmo_regions": ["I"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(307,'','tsunami','2026-11-07T04:17:33Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-05','{"actions": ["National workshop on coastal resilience, science, early warning and youth engagement held for World Tsunami Awareness Day"], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "UN Office for Disaster Risk Reduction (UNDRR)", "type": "international"}, {"country": "LB", "name": "National Council for Scientific Research (CNRS-L)", "type": "other_national_agency"}, {"country": "LB", "name": "National Disaster Risk Management Unit (Lebanon)", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["international", "other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.6, "countries": [{"code": "LB", "name": "Lebanon"}], "event_date": "2026-11-05", "event_location": "Lebanon", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:49Z", "hazard": "tsunami", "hazards": ["tsunami"], "id": 307, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes an awareness workshop; no actual warning event, warning issuance or outcome is reported.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-05T13:58:50Z", "source_name": "UNDRR news", "title": "Lebanon marks World Tsunami Awareness Day with national workshop on coastal resilience, science, and youth engagement", "title_en": "Lebanon marks World Tsunami Awareness Day with national workshop on coastal resilience, science, and youth engagement", "url": "https://www.undrr.org/news/lebanon-marks-world-tsunami-awareness-day-national-workshop-coastal-resilience-science-and"}, {"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T12:33:14Z", "source_name": "ReliefWeb - Updates", "title": "Lebanon marks World Tsunami Awareness Day with national workshop on coastal resilience, science, and youth engagement", "title_en": "Lebanon marks World Tsunami Awareness Day with national workshop on coastal resilience, science, and youth engagement", "url": "https://reliefweb.int/report/lebanon/lebanon-marks-world-tsunami-awareness-day-national-workshop-coastal-resilience-science-and-youth-engagement"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "UNDRR, together with Lebanon''s CNRS-L and National Disaster Risk Management Unit, held a national workshop marking World Tsunami Awareness Day on 5 November 2026. The workshop focused on strengthening coastal resilience through science, early warning and youth engagement. The snippet is truncated and describes no specific warning issued or event.", "title": "Lebanon marks World Tsunami Awareness Day with national workshop on coastal resilience, science, and youth engagement", "wmo_regions": ["II", "VI"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(308,'earthquake|ID|santa ana','earthquake','2026-11-07T04:17:33Z','2026-11-07T04:10:38Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Worldwide action to develop advanced early warning systems for earthquake preparedness was reported"], "agencies": [{"country": "ID", "name": "Badan Nasional Penanggulangan Bencana (BNPB)", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.7, "countries": [{"code": "ID", "name": "Indonesia"}, {"code": "PH", "name": "Philippines"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Santa Ana, Cagayan, Philippines", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:10:38Z", "hazard": "earthquake", "hazards": ["earthquake"], "id": 308, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:10:38Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes efforts to develop earthquake early warning systems but reports no specific warning issued or outcome.", "pillars": [1, 2], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T02:00:00Z", "source_name": "manilatimes.net", "title": "Devt of advanced early warning system for quake underway", "title_en": "Development of advanced early warning system for quake underway", "url": "https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/11/06/regions/devt-of-advanced-early-warning-system-for-quake-underway/2463675"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Indonesia''s Deputy Minister Abdul Muhari of BNPB, speaking at Santa Ana, Cagayan, reported on a worldwide initiative to develop advanced early warning systems for earthquake preparedness. The item concerns the development of earthquake early warning capability rather than a specific warning event. Details on the systems and their deployment are not given in the snippet.", "title": "Development of advanced early warning system for quake underway", "wmo_regions": ["II", "V"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(309,'flood|NP|rasuwa district','flash_flood','2026-11-07T04:17:33Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": [], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "NP", "name": "Nepal"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Rasuwa district, Nepal", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "flash_flood", "hazards": ["flash_flood"], "id": 309, "impacts": {"deaths": 1355}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports the event and its death toll but does not state whether warnings were issued, received, or acted upon; a learning case study implies early warning shortcomings may be examined.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T07:40:54Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Initial learning from the flash flood in the Rasuwa district of Nepal", "title_en": "Initial learning from the flash flood in the Rasuwa district of Nepal", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/initial-learning-flash-flood-rasuwa-district-nepal"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A case study reviews initial lessons from a flash flood on the Bhotekoshi river that swept through Rasuwa district, Nepal, on 26 August 2026. The flood reportedly killed more than 1,355 people. The snippet does not detail the monitoring, forecasts, or warnings that preceded the event, but the framing as a learning document suggests early warning performance is under review.", "title": "Initial learning from the flash flood in the Rasuwa district of Nepal", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(310,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-07T04:17:33Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": [], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "AF", "name": "Afghanistan"}, {"code": "ET", "name": "Ethiopia"}, {"code": "ML", "name": "Mali"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 310, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes lessons and progress on multi-hazard early warning systems in fragile settings but reports no specific warning outcome.", "pillars": [2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T07:44:34Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Lessons in implementing MHEWS in fragile, conflict- and violence-affected contexts", "title_en": "Lessons in implementing MHEWS in fragile, conflict- and violence-affected contexts", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/lessons-implementing-mhews-fragile-conflict-and-violence-affected-contexts"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A case study drawing on experience from Afghanistan, Mali and the Somali region of Ethiopia examines how multi-hazard early warning systems (MHEWS) can be implemented in fragile, conflict- and violence-affected contexts. It argues that meaningful progress on early warning is possible despite resource constraints and insecurity. The item concerns early warning system implementation rather than a specific hazard event.", "title": "Lessons in implementing MHEWS in fragile, conflict- and violence-affected contexts", "wmo_regions": ["I", "II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(311,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-07T04:17:33Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": [], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "HT", "name": "Haiti"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Haiti", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 311, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes a case study on matching warning technology to capacity in Haiti but does not report any specific warning outcome.", "pillars": [2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T07:45:10Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Haiti: Matching warning technology to existing capacity in a fragile context", "title_en": "Haiti: Matching warning technology to existing capacity in a fragile context", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/haiti-matching-warning-technology-existing-capacity-fragile-context"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A PreventionWeb case study examines how early warning technology can be matched to existing capacity in Haiti, a country highly exposed to multiple hazards. The snippet highlights fragile operating conditions including blackouts, security constraints and limited institutional resources that affect warning systems. The item concerns early warning system design and dissemination feasibility rather than a specific event outcome.", "title": "Haiti: Matching warning technology to existing capacity in a fragile context", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(312,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-07T04:17:34Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": [], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.7, "countries": [], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 312, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet discusses the need for monitoring of under-monitored hazards but reports no specific warning outcome.", "pillars": [1, 2], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T09:22:36Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Detection and warning for under-monitored hazards", "title_en": "Detection and warning for under-monitored hazards", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/detection-and-warning-under-monitored-hazards"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "The item highlights extreme heat, wildfires, volcanic eruptions and solar storms as hazards requiring greater investment. It notes that some of these may fall outside national hydrometeorological networks yet still need monitoring. The focus is on detection gaps relevant to early warning systems.", "title": "Detection and warning for under-monitored hazards", "wmo_regions": []}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(313,'','heatwave','2026-11-07T04:17:35Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Co-authored a HEWS Policy Brief with policy recommendations to clarify roles and improve coordination of heat early warning systems"], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "Risk-informed Early Action Partnership (REAP)", "type": "international"}], "agency_types": ["international"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "heatwave", "hazards": ["heatwave"], "id": 313, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item describes a policy brief with recommendations; it reports no warning events or outcomes.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T09:23:21Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Key policy recommendations for effective Heat Early Warning Systems", "title_en": "Key policy recommendations for effective Heat Early Warning Systems", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/key-policy-recommendations-effective-heat-early-warning-systems"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Heat experts from the Risk-informed Early Action Partnership co-authored a Heat Early Warning Systems (HEWS) Policy Brief. The brief aims to clarify roles, improve coordination and enhance resilience as extreme heat becomes an increasingly critical risk. It focuses on policy recommendations for effective heat early warning.", "title": "Key policy recommendations for effective Heat Early Warning Systems", "wmo_regions": []}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(314,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-07T04:17:36Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "Green Climate Fund", "type": "international"}], "agency_types": ["international"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.7, "countries": [{"code": "AG", "name": "Antigua and Barbuda"}, {"code": "EC", "name": "Ecuador"}, {"code": "ET", "name": "Ethiopia"}, {"code": "FJ", "name": "Fiji"}, {"code": "KH", "name": "Cambodia"}, {"code": "SO", "name": "Somalia"}, {"code": "TD", "name": "Chad"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 314, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes a multi-country early warning project''s aims but reports no specific warning events or outcomes.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T09:25:48Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "GCF project: Multi-country project advancing Early Warnings for All (EW4All)", "title_en": "GCF project: Multi-country project advancing Early Warnings for All (EW4All)", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/gcf-project-multi-country-project-advancing-early-warnings-all-ew4all"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "A Green Climate Fund project is working to strengthen community resilience through the Early Warnings for All (EW4All) initiative across seven countries: Ecuador, Chad, Cambodia, Ethiopia, Somalia, Antigua and Barbuda, and Fiji. The item describes project aims rather than a specific hazard event, and no warning outcomes are reported in the snippet.", "title": "GCF project: Multi-country project advancing Early Warnings for All (EW4All)", "wmo_regions": ["I", "II", "III", "IV", "V"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(315,'named|vance','tropical_cyclone','2026-11-07T04:17:36Z','2026-11-07T04:15:31Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Closure of navigation for small vessels in Acapulco and Ixtapa Zihuatanejo"], "agencies": [{"country": "MX", "name": "Mexican Navy (Semar)", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "MX", "name": "Mexico"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Acapulco and Ixtapa Zihuatanejo, Mexico", "event_name": "Hurricane Vance", "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:15:31Z", "hazard": "tropical_cyclone", "hazards": ["tropical_cyclone"], "id": 315, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:15:31Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports the navigation closure decree for Hurricane Vance but gives no information on results or impacts.", "pillars": [3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-06T11:30:00Z", "source_name": "infodefensa.com", "title": "La Armada de México responde a seis huracanes y un frente frío con el Plan Marina en 2026", "title_en": "The Mexican Navy responds to six hurricanes and a cold front with the Plan Marina in 2026", "url": "https://www.infodefensa.com/texto-diario/mostrar/6081202/acciones-plan-marina-2026"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "La Armada de México responde a seis huracanes y un frente frío con el Plan Marina en 2026. Para el huracán Vance, seguido en el Pacífico, se decretó el cierre de la navegación para embarcaciones menores en Acapulco e Ixtapa Zihuatanejo."}, "summary_en": "The Mexican Navy''s Plan Marina 2026 coordinated responses to six hurricanes and a cold front. For Hurricane Vance, tracked in the Pacific, a navigation closure was decreed for small vessels at Acapulco and Ixtapa Zihuatanejo. The snippet gives no further detail on warnings or outcomes.", "title": "The Mexican Navy responds to six hurricanes and a cold front with the Plan Marina in 2026", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(316,'flood|PE|callao','flood','2026-11-07T04:17:37Z','2026-11-07T04:15:51Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": "PE", "name": "Lima Airport Partners (LAP)", "type": "other"}], "agency_types": ["other"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.7, "countries": [{"code": "PE", "name": "Peru"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Callao, Peru", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:15:51Z", "hazard": "flood", "hazards": ["flood"], "id": 316, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:15:51Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item reports a flood risk warning issued by the airport operator; no outcome of the warning is described.", "pillars": [1, 2], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-06T13:07:11Z", "source_name": "La República (Perú) sociedad", "title": "Aeropuerto Jorge Chávez: LAP alerta riesgo de inundaciones por crecida del río Rímac", "title_en": "Jorge Chávez Airport: LAP warns of flood risk from Rímac River rise", "url": "https://larepublica.pe/sociedad/2026/11/06/aeropuerto-jorge-chavez-lap-alerta-riesgo-de-inundaciones-por-crecida-del-rio-rimac-337266"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "El operador del Aeropuerto Jorge Chávez advirtió que una eventual crecida del río Rímac podría afectar la avenida Néstor Gambetta, sectores de la segunda pista y sistemas eléctricos y de comunicaciones."}, "summary_en": "The operator of Lima''s Jorge Chávez International Airport warned that a possible rise in the Rímac River flow could flood Néstor Gambetta avenue and parts of the second runway, and affect electrical and communication systems. The warning highlights risk knowledge and hazard awareness ahead of a possible river rise, though no official forecast or dissemination details are given in the snippet.", "title": "Jorge Chávez Airport: LAP warns of flood risk from Rímac River rise", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(317,'','drought','2026-11-07T04:17:37Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Use of a Water Resource Tool to forecast water availability", "Supporting early action for drought preparedness", "Developing a national anticipatory action framework"], "agencies": [{"country": "TV", "name": "Government of Tuvalu", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [{"code": "TV", "name": "Tuvalu"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Tuvalu", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "drought", "hazards": ["drought"], "id": 317, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes preparedness and tool development but reports no realised outcomes of warnings.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T14:24:56Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "From water data to anticipatory action for drought in Tuvalu", "title_en": "From water data to anticipatory action for drought in Tuvalu", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/water-data-anticipatory-action-drought-tuvalu"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Tuvalu has strengthened drought preparedness through a Water Resource Tool that forecasts water availability and supports early action. The country is also improving its multi-hazard early warning systems and developing a national anticipatory action framework.", "title": "From water data to anticipatory action for drought in Tuvalu", "wmo_regions": ["V"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(318,'','glacial_lake_outburst','2026-11-07T04:17:37Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Early action taken during glacial lake flood threats to protect communities and infrastructure"], "agencies": [{"country": "KG", "name": "Kyrgyz national hydrometeorological service", "type": "NMHS"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [{"code": "KG", "name": "Kyrgyzstan"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Kyrgyzstan", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "glacial_lake_outburst", "hazards": ["glacial_lake_outburst"], "id": 318, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "positive", "outcome_justification": "Snippet states the investments enabled effective early action that helped protect communities and infrastructure.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T14:25:15Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Anticipating high-mountain lake outbursts through an integrated national warning system in Kyrgyzstan", "title_en": "Anticipating high-mountain lake outbursts through an integrated national warning system in Kyrgyzstan", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/anticipating-high-mountain-lake-outbursts-through-integrated-national-warning"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Kyrgyzstan has built a multi-hazard early warning system improving monitoring, forecasting and alerts for high-mountain lake outbursts. According to the case study, these investments enabled effective early action during glacial lake flood threats, helping protect communities and infrastructure.", "title": "Anticipating high-mountain lake outbursts through an integrated national warning system in Kyrgyzstan", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(319,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-07T04:17:38Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["National multi-hazard early warning system planning", "Strengthening risk data and weather and health monitoring", "Community-based flood early warning systems"], "agencies": [], "agency_types": [], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "YE", "name": "Yemen"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Yemen", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 319, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes efforts to advance early warning systems but reports no specific outcome of warnings issued during an event.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T14:25:34Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Advancing early warning and resilience in a protracted crisis in Yemen", "title_en": "Advancing early warning and resilience in a protracted crisis in Yemen", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/advancing-early-warning-and-resilience-protracted-crisis-yemen"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Despite conflict and limited resources, Yemen is advancing its multi-hazard early warning systems through national planning, improved risk data, and weather and health monitoring. Community-based flood early warning systems are also being developed to strengthen preparedness and resilience in a highly fragile context.", "title": "Advancing early warning and resilience in a protracted crisis in Yemen", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(320,'','flood','2026-11-07T04:17:38Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Launched a Community Flood Early Warning System linking river monitoring, alerts and local responders", "Strengthened preparedness and anticipatory action in flood-prone communities"], "agencies": [{"country": "TT", "name": "Government of Trinidad and Tobago", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [{"code": "TT", "name": "Trinidad and Tobago"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Trinidad and Tobago", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "flood", "hazards": ["flood"], "id": 320, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "positive", "outcome_justification": "The snippet states the system has strengthened preparedness and anticipatory action in flood-prone communities, though no specific lives saved or losses reduced are quantified.", "pillars": [2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T14:25:57Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Insights from implementing a community flood early warning system in Trinidad and Tobago", "title_en": "Insights from implementing a community flood early warning system in Trinidad and Tobago", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/insights-implementing-community-flood-early-warning-system-trinidad-and-tobago"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Following the 2018 floods, which exposed gaps in warnings, Trinidad and Tobago launched a Community Flood Early Warning System linking river monitoring, alerts and local responders. The system is reported to have strengthened preparedness and anticipatory action in flood-prone communities.", "title": "Insights from implementing a community flood early warning system in Trinidad and Tobago", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(321,'','tsunami','2026-11-07T04:17:38Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["timely tsunami warnings issued", "evacuation of more than 2,300 people", "coordinated response actions", "regular drills conducted after the 2016 earthquake"], "agencies": [{"country": "EC", "name": "Ecuador multi-hazard early warning system", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": ["cell_broadcast", "sms", "social_media"], "confidence": 0.95, "countries": [{"code": "EC", "name": "Ecuador"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "tsunami", "hazards": ["tsunami"], "id": 321, "impacts": {"evacuated": 2300}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "positive", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports that the strengthened system enabled timely warnings, evacuation of 2,300+ people and coordinated action during the 2025 tsunami threat.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T14:26:16Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Adapting MHEWS in response to a tsunami threat in Ecuador", "title_en": "Adapting MHEWS in response to a tsunami threat in Ecuador", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/adapting-mhews-response-tsunami-threat-ecuador"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Following the 2016 earthquake, Ecuador strengthened its multi-hazard early warning system with clear protocols, multichannel alerts and regular drills. During a 2025 tsunami threat, the system enabled timely warnings and the evacuation of more than 2,300 people, with coordinated action across agencies.", "title": "Adapting MHEWS in response to a tsunami threat in Ecuador", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(322,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-07T04:17:39Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Launched Emergency Operations and Communication Centre in 2024 with UNDRR support", "Issued over 200 advisories by 2026", "Strengthened multi-hazard early warning and improved preparedness"], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "UNDRR", "type": "international"}, {"country": "TZ", "name": "Emergency Operations and Communication Centre (EOCC), Tanzania", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["international", "other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "TZ", "name": "Tanzania"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": null, "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 322, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "positive", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports that the EOCC issued 200+ advisories and strengthened multi-hazard early warning and preparedness following coordination gaps exposed by 2023-2024 El Niño floods, but no specific lives saved or losses reduced are quantified.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T14:26:38Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Strengthening coordination through the Emergency Operations and Communication Centre in the United Republic of Tanzania", "title_en": "Strengthening coordination through the Emergency Operations and Communication Centre in the United Republic of Tanzania", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/strengthening-coordination-through-emergency-operations-and-communication"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Following severe El Niño floods in 2023-2024 that exposed coordination and data-sharing gaps, Tanzania launched its Emergency Operations and Communication Centre in 2024 with UNDRR support. By 2026 the centre had issued more than 200 advisories and strengthened multi-hazard early warning and preparedness. The case study focuses on improving institutional coordination for early warning.", "title": "Strengthening coordination through the Emergency Operations and Communication Centre in the United Republic of Tanzania", "wmo_regions": ["I"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(323,'flood|LV|zemgale region','flood','2026-11-07T04:17:39Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": ["Extension of city early warning system to the entire Zemgale region"], "agencies": [{"country": "LV", "name": "Jelgava city early warning system", "type": "other"}], "agency_types": ["other"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "LV", "name": "Latvia"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Zemgale Region, Latvia", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "flood", "hazards": ["flood"], "id": 323, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes the expansion of an early warning system for river and flash floods but does not report results or outcomes of warnings.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T16:11:59Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Combining GIS, hydraulic modelling and public safety: an early warning system for flood risk management in Zemgale Region (Latvia)", "title_en": "Combining GIS, hydraulic modelling and public safety: an early warning system for flood risk management in Zemgale Region (Latvia)", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/resource/case-study/combining-gis-hydraulic-modelling-and-public-safety-early-warning-system-flood"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "The early warning system operating in Jelgava city has been extended to cover the entire Zemgale region in Latvia, which is highly exposed to river and flash floods. The case study combines GIS, hydraulic modelling and public safety approaches to flood risk management. The snippet does not report outcomes of warnings issued.", "title": "Combining GIS, hydraulic modelling and public safety: an early warning system for flood risk management in Zemgale Region (Latvia)", "wmo_regions": ["VI"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(324,'','multi_hazard','2026-11-07T04:17:39Z','2026-11-07T04:09:50Z','2026-11-06','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": null, "name": "PreventionWeb", "type": "other"}], "agency_types": ["other"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.6, "countries": [{"code": "ID", "name": "Indonesia"}], "event_date": "2026-11-06", "event_location": "Indonesia", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "hazard": "multi_hazard", "hazards": ["multi_hazard"], "id": 324, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:09:50Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The report is a risk analysis; it recommends integrated early warning systems but does not describe warnings issued or their outcomes.", "pillars": [1, 2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-06T16:51:51Z", "source_name": "PreventionWeb", "title": "Climate risks to health and nutrition in Indonesia: Targeted analytics", "title_en": "Climate risks to health and nutrition in Indonesia: Targeted analytics", "url": "https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/climate-risks-health-and-nutrition-indonesia-targeted"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "This report maps climate hazards and health facility exposure in Indonesia and estimates over 3.6 million additional cases of five climate-sensitive conditions by 2050. It recommends resilient health services and integrated early warning systems to reduce these health risks.", "title": "Climate risks to health and nutrition in Indonesia: Targeted analytics", "wmo_regions": ["II", "V"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(325,'severe_storm|JP|northern japan (hokkaido and tohoku)','severe_storm','2026-11-07T04:17:39Z','2026-11-07T04:10:54Z','2026-11-07','{"actions": ["Issuance of gale, high wave and heavy snow warnings/cautions for northern Japan"], "agencies": [{"country": "JP", "name": "Japan Meteorological Agency", "type": "NMHS"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS"], "channels": ["website"], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "JP", "name": "Japan"}], "event_date": "2026-11-07", "event_location": "Northern Japan (Hokkaido and Tohoku), Japan", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:10:54Z", "hazard": "severe_storm", "hazards": ["severe_storm"], "id": 325, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["ja"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:10:54Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes warnings and cautions being issued for the coming days but reports no outcomes yet.", "pillars": [2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-11-07T02:54:00Z", "source_name": "NHK ニュース 主要", "title": "冬型強まり北日本中心に暴風警戒 大雪に十分注意を", "title_en": "Strong winter pressure pattern brings gale warnings mainly to northern Japan; heavy snow caution", "url": "https://news.web.nhk/newsweb/na/nd-20261107de72009"}], "summaries_original": {"ja": "強い冬型の気圧配置の影響で、北日本では雪を伴って非常に強い風が吹いている。8日にかけて風の強い状態が続き、北海道の日本海側では大雪のおそれがあるため、暴風や高波、大雪への警戒が呼びかけられている。"}, "summary_en": "A strong winter pressure pattern is bringing strong winds and snow to northern Japan. Gale and high wave warnings are in place, and heavy snow is possible on Hokkaido''s Sea of Japan coast through 8 November, with residents urged to take caution.", "title": "Strong winter pressure pattern brings gale warnings mainly to northern Japan; heavy snow caution", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(326,'flood|CO|medellin','flash_flood','2026-11-07T04:17:40Z','2026-11-07T04:15:38Z','2026-11-07','{"actions": [], "agencies": [{"country": "CO", "name": "SIATA (Sistema de Alerta Temprana de Medellín y el Valle de Aburrá)", "type": "other_national_agency"}, {"country": "CO", "name": "Secretaría de Movilidad de Medellín", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [{"code": "CO", "name": "Colombia"}], "event_date": "2026-11-07", "event_location": "Medellín, Colombia", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-07T04:15:38Z", "hazard": "flash_flood", "hazards": ["flash_flood"], "id": 326, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-07T04:15:38Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports SIATA monitoring showing La Presidenta creek reached red level and a traffic agency reporting waterlogging, but gives no information on warning dissemination, actions taken or outcomes.", "pillars": [2], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": "2026-11-07T04:15:31Z", "source_name": "elespectador.com", "title": "Emergencia por fuertes lluvias en Medellín: reportan inundaciones y quebradas en alerta roja", "title_en": "Emergency due to heavy rain in Medellín: floods and creeks on red alert reported", "url": "https://www.elespectador.com/colombia/medellin/emergencia-por-fuertes-lluvias-en-medellin-reportan-inundaciones-y-quebradas-en-alerta-roja/?outputType=amp"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "Según SIATA, la quebrada La Presidenta alcanzó nivel rojo tras las fuertes lluvias del 5 de noviembre, y la Secretaría de Movilidad reportó un encharcamiento en la calle 29 con carrera 44."}, "summary_en": "SIATA, Medellín and the Aburrá Valley''s early warning system reported that the La Presidenta creek reached red alert level after heavy rains on 5 November. The city''s mobility secretariat reported waterlogging at a street intersection. The snippet does not describe warnings issued to the public or any response.", "title": "Emergency due to heavy rain in Medellín: floods and creeks on red alert reported", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(327,'other|PE|central and southern jungle','other','2026-11-08T04:17:00Z','2026-11-08T04:15:57Z','2026-11-08','{"actions": ["INDECI recommends preparedness measures in response to SENAMHI Meteorological Warning No. 461 (orange level)"], "agencies": [{"country": "PE", "name": "SENAMHI", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "PE", "name": "INDECI", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS", "other_national_agency"], "channels": ["other"], "confidence": 0.95, "countries": [{"code": "PE", "name": "Peru"}], "event_date": "2026-11-08", "event_location": "Central and southern jungle, Peru", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-08T04:15:57Z", "hazard": "other", "hazards": ["other"], "id": 327, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-08T04:15:57Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item announces recommended preparedness measures for a warned wind event but reports no outcome.", "pillars": [3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": null, "source_name": "INDECI Perú noticias", "title": "INDECI recomienda medidas de preparación ante el incremento de la velocidad del viento en la selva centro y sur - décimo quinto friaje", "title_en": "INDECI recommends preparedness measures for increased wind speed in the central and southern jungle - fifteenth friaje", "url": "https://www.gob.pe/institucion/indeci/noticias/1471047-indeci-recomienda-medidas-de-preparacion-ante-el-incremento-de-la-velocidad-del-viento-en-la-selva-centro-y-sur-decimo-quinto-friaje"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "INDECI recomienda adoptar medidas de preparación ante el Aviso Meteorológico N.° 461 (nivel naranja) del SENAMHI, que informa sobre el incremento de la velocidad del viento de moderada a fuerte en la selva centro y sur durante el décimo quinto friaje."}, "summary_en": "INDECI issued a press release recommending preparedness measures following SENAMHI''s orange-level Meteorological Warning No. 461, which reports increasing moderate-to-strong wind speeds in the central and southern Peruvian jungle during the fifteenth friaje of the season. The item focuses on warning communication and preparedness advice rather than observed impacts.", "title": "INDECI recommends preparedness measures for increased wind speed in the central and southern jungle - fifteenth friaje", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(328,'cold_wave|PE|central and southern selva','cold_wave','2026-11-08T04:17:00Z','2026-11-08T04:15:57Z','2026-11-08','{"actions": ["INDECI recommends preparedness measures in response to SENAMHI Aviso N.° 459 (orange level)"], "agencies": [{"country": "PE", "name": "SENAMHI", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "PE", "name": "INDECI", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS", "other_national_agency"], "channels": ["other"], "confidence": 0.95, "countries": [{"code": "PE", "name": "Peru"}], "event_date": "2026-11-08", "event_location": "Central and southern selva, Peru", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-08T04:15:57Z", "hazard": "cold_wave", "hazards": ["cold_wave"], "id": 328, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["es"], "last_updated": "2026-11-08T04:15:57Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes recommended preparedness measures and a SENAMHI warning but reports no outcome.", "pillars": [2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "es", "published_at": null, "source_name": "INDECI Perú noticias", "title": "INDECI recomienda medidas de preparación ante el descenso de la temperatura diurna en la selva centro y sur - décimo quinto friaje", "title_en": "INDECI recommends preparedness measures ahead of daytime temperature drop in central and southern jungle - fifteenth friaje", "url": "https://www.gob.pe/institucion/indeci/noticias/1471046-indeci-recomienda-medidas-de-preparacion-ante-el-descenso-de-la-temperatura-diurna-en-la-selva-centro-y-sur-decimo-quinto-friaje"}], "summaries_original": {"es": "INDECI recomienda adoptar medidas de preparación ante el Aviso N.° 459 (nivel naranja) del SENAMHI, que informa sobre el descenso de la temperatura diurna, de moderada a fuerte intensidad, en la selva centro y sur del país, décimo quinto friaje."}, "summary_en": "INDECI, Peru''s civil defence institute, recommends preparedness measures following SENAMHI Warning No. 459 (orange level) for a moderate-to-strong drop in daytime temperature (friaje) in the central and southern jungle. This is the fifteenth friaje event of the season. The item concerns the dissemination of a meteorological warning and related preparedness advice.", "title": "INDECI recommends preparedness measures ahead of daytime temperature drop in central and southern jungle - fifteenth friaje", "wmo_regions": ["III"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(329,'flood|CA|zeballos','heavy_rain','2026-11-08T04:17:01Z','2026-11-08T04:10:57Z','2026-11-07','{"actions": ["Evacuation of 22 properties ordered by the Village of Zeballos due to landslide risk", "State of local emergency declared over northern Vancouver Island"], "agencies": [{"country": "CA", "name": "Village of Zeballos", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": [], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [{"code": "CA", "name": "Canada"}], "event_date": "2026-11-07", "event_location": "Zeballos, Vancouver Island, Canada", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-08T04:10:57Z", "hazard": "heavy_rain", "hazards": ["heavy_rain"], "id": 329, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-08T04:10:57Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet reports evacuation orders and forecasts of further systems but does not state outcomes of the warnings.", "pillars": [3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-07T04:10:52Z", "source_name": "cp24.com", "title": "B.C. storm triggers evacuations, warnings", "title_en": "B.C. storm triggers evacuations, warnings", "url": "https://www.cp24.com/news/canada/2026/11/06/evacuations-and-state-of-local-emergency-over-drenching-bc-rain/"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "Evacuations were ordered for 22 properties in the Village of Zeballos on northern Vancouver Island due to landslide risks from drenching rain, and a state of local emergency was declared. Forecasters warned that more weather systems are expected over the following week.", "title": "B.C. storm triggers evacuations, warnings", "wmo_regions": ["IV"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(330,'tropical_cyclone|JP|south of japan','tropical_cyclone','2026-11-08T04:17:01Z','2026-11-10T04:12:41Z','2026-11-07','{"actions": ["JMA called on the public to pay attention to future information"], "agencies": [{"country": "JP", "name": "Japan Meteorological Agency (JMA)", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Kyoto Shimbun", "type": "media"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS", "media"], "channels": ["other", "website"], "confidence": 0.9, "countries": [{"code": "JP", "name": "Japan"}], "event_date": "2026-11-07", "event_location": null, "event_name": "Typhoon No. 32 (2026)", "first_seen": "2026-11-08T04:11:05Z", "hazard": "tropical_cyclone", "hazards": ["tropical_cyclone"], "id": 330, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["ja"], "last_updated": "2026-11-10T04:12:41Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The item is a JMA follow-up forecast commentary on a strong typhoon moving eastward; no impacts or responses are reported in the snippet.", "pillars": [2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-11-07T04:44:34Z", "source_name": "NHK ニュース 社会", "title": "台風32号が発生 年間発生数は1994年以来の多さに", "title_en": "Typhoon No. 32 forms; annual number of typhoons highest since 1994", "url": "https://news.web.nhk/newsweb/na/nd-20261107de72096"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-11-10T03:30:00Z", "source_name": "kyoto-np.co.jp", "title": "全般気象解説情報 （ 台風第３２号 ）（ 第３報 ） ＝気象庁発表 （ １０日４時４８分 ） ： 気象解説情報｜京都新聞デジタル 京都 ・ 滋賀のニュースサイト", "title_en": "General Weather Commentary (Typhoon No. 32) (3rd report) — issued by JMA at 04:48 on 10 November", "url": "https://www.kyoto-np.co.jp/articles/-/1823283"}], "summaries_original": {"ja": "気象庁は強い台風第32号について第3報となる全般気象解説情報を発表し、台風は11日にかけて東寄りに進む見通しを伝えた。"}, "summary_en": "JMA issued the third general weather commentary on Typhoon No. 32, a strong typhoon expected to move eastward over the coming day. The report, relayed by Kyoto Shimbun, is a forecast advisory from the national meteorological service.", "title": "General Weather Commentary (Typhoon No. 32) (3rd report) — issued by JMA at 04:48 on 10 November", "wmo_regions": ["II", "V"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(331,'earthquake|JP|western shizuoka prefecture','earthquake','2026-11-08T04:17:02Z','2026-11-08T04:11:05Z','2026-11-07','{"actions": ["Provisional operation of landslide-related warnings and advisories following the earthquake", "JMA stated that, based on the earthquake''s mechanism and magnitude, the plate boundary where a Nankai Trough megaquake could occur showed no particular abnormality", "JMA advised of possible similar shaking for about one week"], "agencies": [{"country": "JP", "name": "Japan Meteorological Agency", "type": "NMHS"}, {"country": "JP", "name": "Japan Meteorological Agency (JMA)", "type": "NMHS"}], "agency_types": ["NMHS"], "channels": ["mobile_app", "other", "tv", "website"], "confidence": 0.85, "countries": [{"code": "JP", "name": "Japan"}], "event_date": "2026-11-07", "event_location": "Western Shizuoka Prefecture, Japan", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-08T04:11:04Z", "hazard": "earthquake", "hazards": ["earthquake"], "id": 331, "impacts": {"injured": 3}, "languages": ["ja"], "last_updated": "2026-11-08T04:11:05Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "mixed", "outcome_justification": "The item is an official JMA press release announcing a provisional operation of warnings; no outcomes are reported in the title.", "pillars": [2, 3], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-11-07T15:00:00Z", "source_name": "気象庁 (JMA)", "title": "令和８年11月８日01時04分頃の静岡県西部の地震に伴う土砂災害に関する警報等の暫定的な運用について", "title_en": "Provisional operation of warnings related to landslide disasters following the earthquake in western Shizuoka Prefecture at around 01:04 on 8 November 2026", "url": "https://www.jma.go.jp/jma/press/2611/08b/20261108_zantei.html"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-11-07T15:00:00Z", "source_name": "気象庁 (JMA)", "title": "令和８年11月８日01時04分頃の静岡県西部の地震について", "title_en": "Regarding the earthquake in western Shizuoka Prefecture at about 01:04 on November 8, 2026", "url": "https://www.jma.go.jp/jma/press/2611/08a/202611080305.html"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-11-08T03:06:27Z", "source_name": "NHK ニュース 主要", "title": "震度5強 愛知で観測約30年ぶり 1週間ほど同程度の揺れに注意", "title_en": "Seismic intensity 5-upper observed in Aichi for first time in about 30 years; similar shaking possible for about a week", "url": "https://news.web.nhk/newsweb/na/nd-20261108de72252"}, {"language": "ja", "published_at": "2026-11-08T03:40:00Z", "source_name": "朝日新聞 (Asahi Shimbun)", "title": "静岡県内では3人がけが 深夜の緊急地震速報に釣り人「パニックに」", "title_en": "Three injured in Shizuoka Prefecture; anglers ''panicked'' by late-night earthquake early warning", "url": "http://www.asahi.com/articles/ASVC80FVWVC8UTPB003M.html?ref=rss"}], "summaries_original": {"ja": "令和8年11月8日01時04分頃に発生した静岡県西部の地震に伴う土砂災害に関する警報等について、暫定的な運用を行うことを発表した気象庁の報道発表です。"}, "summary_en": "JMA announced the provisional operation of landslide disaster warnings and related alerts following an earthquake in western Shizuoka Prefecture at about 01:04 on 8 November 2026. The release concerns how warnings for earthquake-triggered landslide risk are issued during the interim period. The snippet is empty, so specific warning levels and dissemination details cannot be confirmed.", "title": "Provisional operation of warnings related to landslide disasters following the earthquake in western Shizuoka Prefecture at around 01:04 on 8 November 2026", "wmo_regions": ["II"]}');
INSERT INTO "stories" VALUES(332,'','wildfire','2026-11-08T04:17:02Z','2026-11-08T04:11:04Z','2026-11-07','{"actions": ["Raised wildfire prevention measures to maximum alert status", "Began deploying forest protection personnel", "Training forest rangers"], "agencies": [{"country": "PH", "name": "Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)", "type": "other_national_agency"}], "agency_types": ["other_national_agency"], "channels": ["other"], "confidence": 0.8, "countries": [{"code": "PH", "name": "Philippines"}], "event_date": "2026-11-07", "event_location": "Philippines", "event_name": null, "first_seen": "2026-11-08T04:11:04Z", "hazard": "wildfire", "hazards": ["wildfire"], "id": 332, "impacts": {}, "languages": ["en"], "last_updated": "2026-11-08T04:11:04Z", "lead_time": null, "outcome": "not_reported", "outcome_justification": "The snippet describes alert status and preparedness deployments but reports no outcome of the warnings.", "pillars": [2, 3, 4], "review": false, "sources": [{"language": "en", "published_at": "2026-11-07T17:31:54Z", "source_name": "Philippine Daily Inquirer", "title": "DENR on maximum alert vs wildfires amid ‘very strong’ El Niño", "title_en": "DENR on maximum alert vs wildfires amid ''very strong'' El Niño", "url": "https://newsinfo.inquirer.net/2337675/denr-on-maximum-alert-vs-wildfires-amid-very-strong-el-nino"}], "summaries_original": {}, "summary_en": "The Philippine DENR raised its wildfire prevention measures to maximum alert amid extreme heat and dry conditions linked to a ''very strong'' El Niño. The agency announced deployment of forest protection personnel and training of forest rangers in response to the threat.", "title": "DENR on maximum alert vs wildfires amid ''very strong'' El Niño", "wmo_regions": ["II", "V"]}');
